d-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#regenerate","content":"The new helper now has an entry in its module's reference page and a row in All commands. `nb.docs(nb.your_helper)` opens it once the site is rebuilt."},"117":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/add-a-command#test","content":"A whole new module gets its own reference page automatically, titled from its file name. Give it a proper title and a place in the order by adding one line to `PAGES` in `tools/nb_docs.py`."},"118":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"page","content":"These docs","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","For developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site"},"119":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","content":"How this documentation is written, built and shipped, and how to change a page."},"120":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"121":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#change-a-page","content":"Change a page"},"122":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#edit","content":"Edit"},"123":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#preview-while-you-write","content":"Preview while you write"},"124":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#build-and-publish","content":"Build and publish"},"125":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#check","content":"Check"},"126":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#pages-you-do-not-edit","content":"Pages you do not edit"},"127":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#links","content":"Links"},"128":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"**Source:** MDX pages in `notebook/docs/content/docs/`, one folder per persona. The folder layout is the sidebar; each folder's `meta.json` sets its title and page order, and a persona's folder is marked `\"root\": true`, which makes it an entry in the list at the top of the sidebar."},"129":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"**Build:** a static site built with Node on a maintainer's machine. Users never need Node."},"130":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"**Shipped:** the built files, in `notebook/docs/site/`, travel with the kit."},"131":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"**Served:** `nb.docs()` serves that folder from the kit's own Python, on this computer only."},"132":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#how-it-works","content":"Search runs in the browser on an index inside the site. It forgives typos, matches as you type and needs no internet."},"133":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#edit","content":"Edit an `.mdx` file, or add one and list it in its folder's `meta.json`. Each page starts with:"},"134":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#edit","content":"`Callout`, `Tabs`, `Steps`, `Cards` and `Accordions` are available on every page without imports."},"135":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#preview-while-you-write","content":"Run both in `notebook/docs`. The site is at `http://localhost:3000/docs` and reloads on every save."},"136":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#build-and-publish","content":"The first writes `notebook/docs/out`; the second copies it to `notebook/docs/site` and stamps it with a digest of the sources."},"137":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#check","content":"It fails when a generated page is stale, or when the shipped site was built from older sources than the ones in the repository."},"138":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#pages-you-do-not-edit","content":"Everything under a persona's `reference/` folder is generated from the docstrings in `exakit_nb` by `python3 tools/nb_docs.py`. To change a command's text, change its docstring and run the tool."},"139":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/docs-site#links","content":"Link to a page by its address, without the `/docs` prefix and without `.mdx`: `/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor`. Link to a command by its page and name: `/data-scientist/reference/describe#describe`. A test fails on a link that leads nowhere."},"140":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"page","content":"How it fits together","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","For developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits"},"141":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","content":"The helpers, the guided cards and the kit - which part owns what, and the rules that keep them honest."},"142":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"Three layers"},"143":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"The helpers"},"144":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-guided-view","content":"The guided view"},"145":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"Rules the tests enforce"},"146":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#notebooks","content":"Notebooks"},"147":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"Layer"},"148":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"Where"},"149":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"What it owns"},"150":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"The kit"},"151":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"`setup/`, the `exakit` command"},"152":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"The database, connections, loading, connectors, add-ons, the describe service"},"153":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"The helpers"},"154":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"`notebook/package/exakit_nb/` (`import exakit.nb as nb`)"},"155":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"One Python call for each thing a notebook does"},"156":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"The guided view"},"157":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"`notebook/package/exakit_guide/` (`exakit.guide`)"},"158":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"Cards that call the helpers; UI only"},"159":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#three-layers","content":"A notebook is cells that call the helpers. A card is a form that calls the same helpers. Neither talks to the database on its own."},"160":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"`exakit.nb` exports about 110 names, listed in All commands. The rules they follow:"},"161":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"**The connection comes from the kit.** `nb.connect()` opens it from the kit's encrypted store. No helper prints or returns a host, a user or a password."},"162":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"**The kit does the work.** Describing a table is the kit's describe service; loading is `exakit data-load`; connecting a source is `exakit connect`. The helpers call these, they do not reimplement them."},"163":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"**SQL is shown.** `nb.sql` records the statement, `nb.show_sql()` prints it, and the workflow logs it."},"164":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-helpers","content":"**Reads are live.** `nb.components()`, `nb.addons()`, `nb.connectors()` and the rest ask the kit when called."},"165":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#the-guided-view","content":"`actions.code(id, **values)` is the exact cell text. `actions.run(id, **values)` runs that text in the notebook's namespace and logs it. A screen changes nothing except through `actions.run`, which is why **Code** can always show what a card did."},"166":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"An action's call exists in its notebook's code section, and calls something `exakit.nb` exports."},"167":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"No screen names a dataset, connector, add-on or notebook. Those are read from the kit."},"168":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"No action shows a secret: a key is bound at run time, never written into the code."},"169":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#rules-the-tests-enforce","content":"Every exported helper has a page in these docs, and every link in them leads somewhere."},"170":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/how-it-fits#notebooks","content":"Sources are `notebook/notebooks/<persona>/<NN>_<name>.py` in jupytext percent format. The `.ipynb` and the Marimo version are built from them:"},"171":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live","type":"page","content":"Where things live","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","For developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live"},"172":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live","content":"The files and folders the notebooks read and write on this computer."},"173":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live#in-the-database","content":"In the database"},"174":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/develop/where-things-live#what-an-update-touches","content":"What an update touches"},"175":{"id":"/data-scientist/develop/wher