hat-approval-checks-and-writes","content":"The active workflow's log gets one line."},"344":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-77","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#versions","content":"Every approval is a new version. Nothing is overwritten."},"345":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-78","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#versions","content":"Approving an older version's roles again brings it back as the newest version."},"346":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor-79","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/descriptor#reference","content":"`nb.describe`, `nb.Draft`, `nb.review_roles`, `nb.show_roles`, `nb.column_map_versions`, `nb.DescriptorNotApproved`."},"347":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"page","content":"Prepared views","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views"},"348":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","content":"Data checks, linked tables and the typed, cleaned view - how the data is prepared without ever changing your table."},"349":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#is-the-data-clean","content":"Is the data clean?"},"350":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#linked-tables","content":"Linked tables"},"351":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#a-typed-cleaned-view","content":"A typed, cleaned view"},"352":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"Columns that give the answer away"},"353":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#reference","content":"Reference"},"354":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","content":"Step 3, Prepare, looks at the data before anything is computed from it. It never changes your table. What it creates, when you ask, are views in the `EXAKIT_PREPARED` schema."},"355":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#is-the-data-clean","content":"It looks for repeated keys, exact copies, gaps, placeholder values and a rare target. Each finding is one plain sentence that says what it does to a result. Deciding what to do about it is yours."},"356":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#linked-tables","content":"The schema map shows the tables that link to this one, with the evidence for each link. A link adds the other table's columns without adding rows."},"357":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#linked-tables","content":"To correct it: `schema_map.unlink(\"TABLE.COLUMN\")` or `schema_map.link(\"TABLE.COLUMN\", \"TABLE.KEY\")`."},"358":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#linked-tables","content":"The **joined view** combines the table with every linked table. It is a proposal until you create it:"},"359":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#a-typed-cleaned-view","content":"It proposes correct types for numbers and dates stored as text, turns blanks and placeholders into NULL, and removes exact copies. Read what changes before you create it."},"360":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#a-typed-cleaned-view","content":"In `01_explore`, `USE_JOINED = True` and `USE_PREPARED = True` in the first cell create these views and make the later steps read them."},"361":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#columns-that-give-the-answer-away","content":"A column whose values almost decide the target on their own would make a model look better than it is. These columns are listed and left out of the model."},"362":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/prepared-views#reference","content":"Data checks, Schema map and joined view, Typed view."},"363":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"page","content":"Sharing and hand-off","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff"},"364":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","content":"A dashboard that goes up as a preview first, and one folder that lets a colleague repeat the work."},"365":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"A dashboard, preview first"},"366":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"The hand-off bundle"},"367":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-training-handoff","content":"The training handoff"},"368":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#reference","content":"Reference"},"369":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"Step 8 turns one checked result into a dashboard others open in a browser. Dashboards run on **Dash Server**, a kit add-on the notebook installs and starts for you."},"370":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"`nb.share(...)` prepares a dashboard from approved roles and SQL you can read."},"371":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"It goes up as a **preview**. You open it and check that the figures match the query."},"372":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"Only then is it **published**: `dashboard_draft.confirm(dash_server, figures_checked=True)`."},"373":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#a-dashboard-preview-first","content":"A preview that was not checked is never promoted. In automated runs the check is never set, so nothing is published without a person."},"374":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"Step 9 packs the work into one folder and a zip."},"375":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"It is written to `~/.exasol-starter-kit/bundles/<workflow id>/` and holds:"},"376":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"File"},"377":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"What it is"},"378":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`descriptor.yaml`"},"379":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"The approved column map"},"380":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`schema-map.json`"},"381":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"The schema map, when there is one"},"382":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`queries.sql`"},"383":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"Every query the workflow ran, with its digest and row count"},"384":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`workflow.jsonl`"},"385":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"The workflow log as it is"},"386":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"`README.md`"},"387":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"What the data is, which column map version the numbers rest on, what was approved and published, and how to repeat it"},"388":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-hand-off-bundle","content":"Nothing in it is a password."},"389":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#the-training-handoff","content":"The ML Engineer's handoff is a different thing: one JSON file with the feature view, the target and a reproducible split, written by `nb.write_handoff(connection, dataset)` to `~/.exasol-starter-kit/handoffs/`. A stale one is refused, and `nb.handoff_is_stale` names what changed."},"390":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sharing-and-handoff#reference","content":"Share a dashboard, Dash Server tools, Hand-off bundle, Training handoff."},"391":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"page","content":"Sources","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources"},"392":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","content":"The three ways data comes in, and how an external source appears as a schema in your local database."},"393":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-kit-dataset","content":"A kit dataset"},"394":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#your-own-data","content":"Your own data"},"395":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#an-external-source","content":"An external source"},"396":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"A source with several kinds in one"},"397":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#one-source-engine","content":"One source engine"},"398":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"Passwords"},"399":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#live-sources-and-ai","content":"Live sources and AI"},"400":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#reference","content":"Reference"},"401":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","content":"Data reaches the notebooks in three ways. All three end the same way: a table or view the kit can describe, and a column map you approve."},"402":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-kit-dataset","content":"Practice data the kit offers. `tpch`, `energy` and `weather` come with the kit, and `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions` are downloaded when you load them. `nb.sample_datasets()` lists them and says which are loaded."},"403":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#your-own-data","content":"A CSV, Parquet, JSON or Excel file, a folder of them, or a table already in the database. Files are loaded with the kit's own loader, the one `exakit data-load` runs."},"404":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#an-external-source","content":"A database or lake elsewhere: PostgreSQL, MySQL, Snowflake and others. The kit connects it as a **virtual schema**: its tables appear in your local Exasol as `VS_<NAME>` and are read from the source when you query them. Nothing is copied."},"405":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"A **Lakehouse** is one connector for several things: an Iceberg REST catalog, Unity Catalog, AWS Glue, or Parquet files in a plain folder, with the files on S3 or Azure. Two **settings** pick the combination, and each combination asks for different details."},"406":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"In the **Data source** list it appears as a tree, the same one the terminal's connect menu shows:"},"407":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"Pick a **leaf** and both settings are chosen."},"408":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"A setting the tree does not hold, such as the catalog login (token or OAuth), is asked in one more step."},"409":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"Pick **Lakehouse** itself and the settings are asked one by one."},"410":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"In code the settings are plain inputs:"},"411":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#a-source-with-several-kinds-in-one","content":"Some combinations have **two secrets**: the catalog login and the storage keys. The login is asked like any password. The storage secret travels in a file only you can read, removed as soon as the kit has read it."},"412":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#one-source-engine","content":"The connectors, their inputs and the connection-string reader come from the kit's source engine, the one `exakit connect` runs. Nothing about a connector is defined in the notebooks, so a connector added to the kit appears in the form with no notebook change."},"413":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"A password is asked in a hidden box and handed to `exakit connect` on standard input."},"414":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"It is never written into a cell, the code view or the workflow log."},"415":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"A password inside a connection string is used and never shown."},"416":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#passwords","content":"A second secret (a Lakehouse's storage keys) goes to the kit in a private file, never on a command line."},"417":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#live-sources-and-ai","content":"A table from an external source is read from there as you query it. Before sampled rows from a live source go to a model, the notebook names the source and asks. Only a yes sends them."},"418":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/sources#reference","content":"External sources, Your own file or table, Data map."},"419":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"page","content":"Workflow","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow"},"420":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","content":"One id on everything a piece of work does, and the log it leaves."},"421":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#what-is-logged","content":"What is logged"},"422":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#where-the-log-is","content":"Where the log is"},"423":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#no-secrets-in-the-log","content":"No secrets in the log"},"424":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#reference","content":"Reference"},"425":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","content":"A **workflow** gives one id to every query and decision in a piece of work. The quickstart starts it and the other notebooks continue it. You never paste an id."},"426":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","content":"`continue_workflow` takes this kernel's workflow, else the last one started on this computer, and starts a new one only when there is none."},"427":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#what-is-logged","content":"While a workflow is active, every helper that does something appends one line to its log: a SQL statement, a column map draft or approval, a model trace, a dashboard revision, a hand-off. Every guided card action is a line too, with the code it ran and whether it worked."},"428":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#what-is-logged","content":"Without a workflow nothing is written. There are no implicit workflows."},"429":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#where-the-log-is","content":"`~/.exasol-starter-kit/workflows/<id>.jsonl`: one JSON object per line, append-only, readable by you only. The id looks like `wf-20261027-3f9a1c`."},"430":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#no-secrets-in-the-log","content":"A secret-named value or a connection string with a password is refused before anything is written. SQL that looks credential-bearing, such as a statement with a PASSWORD or API_KEY column, is logged with its text replaced and its digest kept, and a warning is shown."},"431":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#no-secrets-in-the-log","content":"A log that cannot be written warns and the cell goes on. Logging never fails the work it describes."},"432":{"id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/concepts/workflow#reference","content":"Workflows."},"433":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"page","content":"Review and approve the column map","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map"},"434":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","content":"Check the roles the kit proposed, correct them, choose the target and approve."},"435":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#open-the-review","content":"Open the review"},"436":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#check-the-uncertain-columns-first","content":"Check the uncertain columns first"},"437":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#correct-roles-and-choose-the-target","content":"Correct roles and choose the target"},"438":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#approve","content":"Approve"},"439":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#read-it-back","content":"Read it back"},"440":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"What you get at the end"},"