gs":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#approve","content":"Press **Approve column map**, or in code:"},"448":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#approve","content":"The first argument is the roles you change, the second the slots. With nothing to change, the saved approval stands."},"449":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"An approved column map. It is saved as a new version, and its roles are published on a view in `EXAKIT_SEMANTIC`. Explore, Ask and Share read only an approved map."},"450":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#after-approving","content":"Approval checks the data again. A warning about a column that gives the target away is not an error: the column stays in the map and is left out of the model."},"451":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/approve-column-map#change-your-mind-later","content":"Open the quickstart, change the roles and approve again. That writes a new version. The other notebooks follow the newest approval when you run their first cell again."},"452":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","type":"page","content":"Ask your data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask"},"453":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","content":"Ask 