 its result. Check the figures against the SQL."},"463":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#approve-and-run","content":"Nothing runs before `approve()`. In the notebook, set `APPROVE_SQL = True` and run the cell again."},"464":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/ask","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/ask#approve-and-run","content":"See AI and tracing and Set up a model."},"465":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"page","content":"Explore and model","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model"},"466":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","content":"Steps 3 to 6 in 01_explore - prepare the data, compare groups, train a baseline model and check it."},"467":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#prepare","content":"Prepare"},"468":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#explore","content":"Explore"},"469":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#model-and-validate","content":"Model and validate"},"470":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"What you 