-and-model-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#model-and-validate","content":"See Model lab."},"478":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#model-and-validate","content":"A dataset with no target skips the model steps and says so. Choose a target in the column map to run them."},"479":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/explore-and-model#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"The data checks, the schema map and the typed view proposal, the group and over-time results with their SQL, a small model with its score, and a note on what the score means."},"480":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","type":"page","content":"Load data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","How-to guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data"},"481":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"Three ways to get data in front of the notebooks - a kit dataset, your own file or table, or an external source."},"482":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data#use-what-you-chose","content":"Use what you chose"},"483":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"What you get at the end"},"484":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"All of this happens in step 1 of `00_quickstart`. On the **Choose your data** card you pick one of three boxes. The code below is what each box runs."},"485":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"A dataset that is not loaded yet is loaded first. Nothing else is needed."},"486":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"A file or a folder:"},"487":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"CSV, Parquet, JSON and Excel work. Leave the schema empty and it is named after the folder: `~/sales-data` becomes `SALES_DATA`."},"488":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"A table that is already in the database:"},"489":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"`nb.data_map(connection)` lists the tables in the database. The kit's own schemas are left out unless you pass `include_kit=True`."},"490":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"The card walks through it one step at a time: an existing connection or a new one, the kind of source, a connection string or manual details, a name, the password, and optional settings."},"491":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"A source with several kinds in one, such as a Lakehouse, shows its choices as a tree under it in the **Data source** list. Pick the catalog and where its files are; the steps after it ask only what that combination needs. See Sources."},"492":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"**Test connection** checks the inputs and reaches the source from this computer. It changes nothing."},"493":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"**Connect and use this data** runs `exakit connect`. The tables then appear as `VS_SALES`."},"494":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","content":"The password is asked in a hidden box. It is never part of the code."},"495":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"`chosen_data` is the table you picked, ready for the column map step."},"496":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"Next: approve the column map."},"497":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/guides/load-data#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"A source on this computer is not `localhost` from the database's point of view. On macOS use `192.168.64.1`. For a cloud source, allow this computer's public IP there; the card shows it."},"498":{"id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","page_id":"/data-scientist/guides/run-the-kit","type":"page","content":"Run 