rl":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"What a row is, from the descriptor's grain: \"one row per order line\" -> \"order lines\" (`one=True`: \"order line\"), \"one row per store and week\" -> \"store weeks\"; at most three words, up to a comma or a word such as \"in\" or \"per\"; \"rows\" when the descriptor does not say."},"997":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-160","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.persona_plan`"},"998":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-161","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"What a persona (this kit's, when not named) brings that is still missing here: `exakit persona plan --json` - \\{persona, datasets\\{loaded, pending}, addons\\{installed, pending, unavailable}, nothing_pending}."},"999":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-162","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.personas`"},"1000":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-163","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The kit's personas (personas/\\*.json): \\{id, title, summary, datasets, addons, visible}."},"1001":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-164","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.prepare_training`"},"1002":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-165","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Refuse stale input, create the view, drop constant features and render the UDF and training SELECT."},"1003":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-166","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.Proposal`"},"1004":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-167","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A question with the SQL proposed for it."},"1005":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-168","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.read_connection_string`"},"1006":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-169","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Read a source's connection string exactly as `exakit connect --url` does: it is handed to the kit's engine (its `paste` command, on standard input, never as an argument)."},"1007":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-170","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.read_handoff`"},"1008":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-171","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The handoff as a dict: from a path to the file, from `<id>-v<n>` (that version's file), or from a descriptor id (the file with the highest version in the handoffs folder)."},"1009":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-172","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.review_roles`"},"1010":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-173","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Profile the loaded sample, file or connected table, show evidence and role choices, then await approval."},"1011":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-174","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.RoleReview`"},"1012":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-175","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"One proposal."},"1013":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-176","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.sample_datasets`"},"1014":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-177","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Every sample dataset this kit ships, in the kit's order: \\{id, label, description, schema, default, loaded, described} - described: it ships a column map, so nb.load_sample opens it ready to use."},"1015":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-178","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.save_descriptor`"},"1016":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-179","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Write a descriptor document as YAML, in the layout of the kit's own descriptor.yaml files - always as schema_version 2: a schema_version 1 document (or one without the record keys) is written as version 1 with `status` (draft unless the document, or `status`, says approved), the owner (EXAKIT_DESCRIPTOR_OWNER, else the OS user), created now, drafted by the user and, when given, `source` (`file:<path>` for a file's descriptor)."},"1017":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-180","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.SchemaMap`"},"1018":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-181","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The schema as found (a draft) or as approved: `doc` holds its tables and links."},"1019":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-182","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.share`"},"1020":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-183","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Make a draft from approved data and inspected SQL; measure=count enables count totals and composition."},"1021":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-184","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.ShareDraft`"},"1022":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-185","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A dashboard prepared from an approved dataset and one query."},"1023":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-186","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.show_roles`"},"1024":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-187","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The descriptor's roles, one per line, as the notebook will use them."},"1025":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-188","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.show_sql`"},"1026":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-189","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Print the last statement sql() ran, so a result can always be traced to the query behind it."},"1027":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-190","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.source_engine`"},"1028":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-191","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Ask the kit's own source engine (setup/virtual-schemas/engine/cli.py, the coordinator behind `exakit connect` and `exakit source`) one of the questions its connect form asks, and return its --json answer:"},"1029":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-192","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.SourceProblem`"},"1030":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-193","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A source cell that cannot go on, said in one short message: no traceback in a notebook."},"1031":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-194","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.SourceTest`"},"1032":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-195","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"What test_source found, one check per line: (what was checked, passed, what it said)."},"1033":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-196","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.sql`"},"1034":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-197","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Run a query and return its rows as a pandas DataFrame; the statement is remembered for show_sql()."},"1035":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-198","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.test_source`"},"1036":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-199","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Test a source before connecting it, changing nothing: first the kit's own check of every input (\\`exakit connect ..."},"1037":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-200","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.themes`"},"1038":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-201","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Sort each side's texts into themes with `endpoint` = (client, model) from nb.model_client(); return the table (a pandas DataFrame when pandas is there, else a list of rows) and print the note."},"1039":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-202","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.trace`"},"1040":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-203","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Group the model calls made inside the block into one trace in the user's own Langfuse project, tagged with the database session, the sample SQL, the workflow id and, given a dataset, its id, descriptor digest and descriptor version (trace_tags)."},"1041":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-204","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.tracing`"},"1042":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-205","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Whether LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY, LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY and LANGFUSE_BASE_URL (or LANGFUSE_HOST) are all set, so trace() records to the user's Langfuse."},"1043":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-206","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.TrainingPlan`"},"1044":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-207","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"What in-database training will run, prepared from an approved, fresh handoff: the feature view and its columns, the script that creates the training UDF, the training SQL and its parameters."},"1045":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-208","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.try_feature`"},"1046":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-209","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Retrain the lab's picked model with `idea` added, on the same split: \\{verdict, text, series}."},"1047":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-210","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.typed_view`"},"1048":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-211","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The proposal for `ds`'s table: its types, its cleaning and the CREATE VIEW, built from the data and the descriptor."},"1049":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-212","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.TypedView`"},"1050":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-213","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The proposal."},"1051":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-214","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.use_mlflow`"},"1052":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-215","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"The MLflow server this kernel records runs to: `tracking_uri` (empty: the kit's own MLflow, or what the shell set); `login=True` asks for the server's username and password (hidden)."},"1053":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-216","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.use_model`"},"1054":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-217","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Your model and Langfuse tracing for this kernel."},"1055":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-218","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.use_table`"},"1056":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-219","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"A table already in the database, to describe next (review_roles): `SCHEMA.TABLE`."},"1057":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-220","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.workflow`"},"1058":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-221","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Start a workflow (a new id, a `start` line in its log) or, with `resume`, continue an existing one."},"1059":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-222","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.workflow_log`"},"1060":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-223","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Every line of a workflow's log, in order."},"1061":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-224","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"`nb.write_handoff`"},"1062":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference-225","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference","content":"Build the handoff (handoff_from) and write it to `$EXAKIT_HOME/handoffs/<id>-v<n>.json` - the folder 0700, the file 0600, replaced whole (a temporary file renamed over it) so a reader never sees half of one."},"1063":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","type":"page","content":"Kit commands","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands"},"1064":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","content":"The kit's own commands, run from a notebook cell with their output shown as it comes - so nobody has to leave the notebook for a terminal to check the kit, update it, install an add-on or load a dataset."},"1065":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#addon_ready","content":"nb.addon_ready"},"1066":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#exakit","content":"nb.exakit"},"1067":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#kit_check","content":"nb.kit_check"},"1068":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#kit_status","content":"nb.kit_status"},"1069":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#kit_update","content":"nb.kit_update"},"1070":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"nb.KitRun"},"1071":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","content":"Every call runs the same `exakit` the terminal runs (on PATH, else in the kit's bin folder), detached from any\nterminal: a question the command would ask takes its default, and a choice is given up front through the variables\nthe command documents (`nb.exakit(\"mcp-setup\", env={\"EXAKIT_MCP_CLIENTS\": \"claude\"})`). Nothing is read from the\nnotebook's input. The result says the exit code and keeps the output, so a cell can test `run.ok`."},"1072":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#addon_ready","content":"Make an add-on usable from here: install it when it is not (`exakit marketplace <addon>`), start it when it\nis a service and stopped (`exakit start <addon>`), and say its state and address. Returns \\{addon, installed,\nstate, url}. An add-on the marketplace does not have is a ValueError; a failed install or start a RuntimeError\n(its output was shown)."},"1073":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#addon_ready","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/03_share`"},"1074":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#exakit","content":"Run `exakit <args>` and show its output line by line as it comes (`show=False` keeps it quiet); the\nKitRun says how it ended. A command that takes longer than `timeout` seconds is stopped and says so."},"1075":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#exakit","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1076":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#kit_check","content":"The kit as it is now, in a few lines: installed or not, the database, each add-on service and its address, the\ndatasets loaded. Never raises: without the command it says where it looked. Returns the status document (\\{} when\nthere is none)."},"1077":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#kit_check","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1078":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#kit_status","content":"`exakit status --json` as a dict."},"1079":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#kit_update","content":"`exakit update` from here (optionally one component: `kit_update(\"notebook\")`). After an update that\ntouched the notebook helpers, restart this kernel so the new ones load; the line printed says so."},"1080":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#kit_update","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1081":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"One command run: the words it was called with, its exit code and everything it printed."},"1082":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"Member"},"1083":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"What it is"},"1084":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`command`"},"1085":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`list[str]`"},"1086":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`code`"},"1087":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`int`"},"1088":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`output`"},"1089":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`str`"},"1090":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`timed_out`"},"1091":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`bool`"},"1092":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`ok`"},"1093":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-commands#KitRun","content":"`lines`"},"1094":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"page","content":"Kit facts","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts"},"1095":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","content":"What the kit has, read live: datasets, connectors, add-ons, AI clients, components, notebooks and personas."},"1096":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#addons","content":"nb.addons"},"1097":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#ai_clients","content":"nb.ai_clients"},"1098":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#components","content":"nb.components"},"1099":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#connector_inputs","content":"nb.connector_inputs"},"1100":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#connectors","content":"nb.connectors"},"1101":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#loaded_files","content":"nb.loaded_files"},"1102":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#notebooks","content":"nb.notebooks"},"1103":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#persona_plan","content":"nb.persona_plan"},"1104":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#personas","content":"nb.personas"},"1105":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#sample_datasets","content":"nb.sample_datasets"},"1106":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","content":"Nothing here is a list typed into the notebook package: each answer is the kit's own - an `exakit ... --json`\ncommand, or a file of the kit copy these notebooks run with (data/datasets/\\*/dataset.conf, notebook/catalog.json,\npersonas/\\*.json, mcp/adapters). The guided view's cards read the same functions, so a card and a cell agree."},"1107":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#addons","content":"The marketplace's add-ons as `exakit marketplace --list --json` reports them: \\{id, name, about, status,\ninstalled, version, url}, and `offered`: False for one the kit's catalog does not offer yet (its\nmarketplace/catalog.json says \"visible\": false, so no marketplace screen lists it)."},"1108":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#addons","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1109":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#ai_clients","content":"The AI clients the kit can connect to the database (its MCP adapters), each \\{id, name, connected}, with\nconnected from `exakit mcp-status --json`."},"1110":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#ai_clients","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1111":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#components","content":"The kit's parts as `exakit version --json` reports them: \\{id, installed, available, status, add_on,\nownership, remedy}, with a status of current, ahead, update_available, available (an add-on not installed) or\nmissing; `available` is the version the kit would install or update to."},"1112":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#components","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1113":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#connector_inputs","content":"What `exakit connect <connector>` asks, from the kit's source engine (`inputs`: what its connect form reads,\nin the form's order). The connector may be named by id or alias. Returns \\{id, name, status, gate, name_input,\ninputs, forms, access, tips, tree, settings, setting_inputs}: `name_input` is the form's first question (the\nsource's name); each of `inputs` is \\{name, label, kind, required, default, choices, secret, file, hint, prompt,\ndraft} - `secret` a password or key (never a cell's text), `file` a path to a file, `hint` the lines the form\nsays above the question. `forms` are the connection-string shapes it reads (`url=`), `access` and `tips`\nwhat its source card says."},"1114":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#connector_inputs","content":"A connector with several kinds of source in one (Lakehouse: Iceberg REST, Unity, Glue or a plain folder, on S3 or\nAzure) has settings that decide what it asks. `tree` is those settings as the connect menu's tree (a catalog,\nand under it the files it can read), each node with the settings its pick gives; give them here\n(`connector_inputs(\"lakehouse\", catalog=\"unity\", files=\"s3\")`) and `inputs` are that combination's.\n`settings` are the ones in force (given, or the kit's default) and `setting_inputs` the setting questions\nthemselves, each with its `choices`, their `choice_labels` and the default in force. Every other connector\nhas an empty `tree` and no `setting_inputs`."},"1115":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#connectors","content":"The kinds of external source `exakit connect` takes, as its own menu lists them (the kit's source engine,\n`catalog`): \\{id, name, summary, aliases, tier, status, version, gate} - `version` the adapter the kit pins,\n`gate` why one is not available yet (empty when it is)."},"1116":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#loaded_files","content":"The files `exakit data-load` put into the database, as the kit records them (its load receipts): one row per\ntable, the latest load - \\{table, rows, file, loaded_at}. A kit dataset (sample_datasets) is not a file here."},"1117":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#loaded_files","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1118":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#notebooks","content":"The kit's notebooks in order (\\{id, persona, step, title, summary, file}), from its notebook catalog; only\n`persona`'s when given. `file` is the path under the notebooks folder (starter-kit-notebooks/...)."},"1119":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#notebooks","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1120":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#persona_plan","content":"What a persona (this kit's, when not named) brings that is still missing here: `exakit persona plan --json`"},"1121":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#persona_plan","content":"\\{persona, datasets\\{loaded, pending}, addons\\{installed, pending, unavailable}, nothing_pending}."},"1122":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#persona_plan","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1123":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#personas","content":"The kit's personas (personas/\\*.json): \\{id, title, summary, datasets, addons, visible}."},"1124":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#sample_datasets","content":"Every sample dataset this kit ships, in the kit's order: \\{id, label, description, schema, default, loaded,\ndescribed} - described: it ships a column map, so nb.load_sample opens it ready to use.\n`loaded` (ids) marks the ones in the database; by default the kit's status says which."},"1125":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/kit-facts#sample_datasets","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1126":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","type":"page","content":"Model lab","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab"},"1127":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","content":"The model lab: nb.model_lab - the Data Scientist chooses the task, the model and the split."},"1128":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#feature_ideas","content":"nb.feature_ideas"},"1129":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"nb.Lab"},"1130":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#lab_data","content":"nb.lab_data"},"1131":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#model_lab","content":"nb.model_lab"},"1132":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#try_feature","content":"nb.try_feature"},"1133":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","content":"Tasks\npredict_yes_no   classification (supervised): the approved 0/1 target\npredict_number   regression (supervised): a number column the user picks\nfind_groups      clustering (unsupervised): no target\nfind_unusual     anomaly detection (unsupervised): no target"},"1134":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","content":"Models are scikit-learn only (already in the kit). \"Compare all\" trains every\nmodel of the task on identical rows and picks the best cross-validated score,\npreferring the simpler model within 0.01. A single model can also be chosen."},"1135":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","content":"The split is the user's: 50-90% for training, by time (newest held out), random\n(stratified for yes/no) or by group (one group never on both sides), with 3, 5\nor 10 cross-validation folds on the training side. Held-out rows are scored once."},"1136":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#feature_ideas","content":"Feature ideas for this lab's data, each with the SQL that would make it: try one with try_feature. With\n`ai`, your AI model (nb.use_model) adds up to four more, of kinds the lab can build and test; it is sent the\ncolumn names, their roles and the scores - never a row or a value - and the call is traced when Langfuse is on\n(`conn` tags the trace with the database session)."},"1137":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#feature_ideas","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1138":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"One model-lab run: the task, its settings, the data it read and what came out (board and pick for a\nprediction, groups or unusual rows otherwise). `features` are the feature ideas it was trained with."},"1139":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"Member"},"1140":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"What it is"},"1141":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`task`"},"1142":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`str`"},"1143":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`model`"},"1144":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`str`"},"1145":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`settings`"},"1146":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`dict`"},"1147":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`data`"},"1148":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`Data`"},"1149":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`run`"},"1150":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`Run`"},"1151":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`result`"},"1152":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`dict`"},"1153":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`target_number`"},"1154":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"\\`str"},"1155":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"None\\`"},"1156":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`features`"},"1157":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`dict[str, pd.Series]`"},"1158":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`note`"},"1159":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`str`"},"1160":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`dataset`"},"1161":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`object`"},"1162":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`board`"},"1163":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`pick`"},"1164":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#Lab","content":"`importance`"},"1165":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#lab_data","content":"The approved data the lab trains on, read once (newest first, at most ROW_LIMIT rows): every usable column,\nwith the ones that give the answer away (nb.leakage_check, unless `leaks` is given) and personal data left out\n(`.left_out` says why). Pass it to model_lab(data=...) to train several times without reading it again."},"1166":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#lab_data","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1167":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#model_lab","content":"Train `task` on the approved dataset: `predict_yes_no` (its target), `predict_number` (`target_number`),\n`find_groups` or `find_unusual`. `model` is one model's key or \"all\" (each of the task, same rows, the\nsimpler one picked within 0.01). `settings` by name: train_pct, split_method (time, random, group),\nsplit_group, folds, effort, max_depth, C, neighbours, learning_rate, clusters, contamination. Columns that give\nthe answer away (nb.leakage_check, unless `leaks` is given) and personal data are left out."},"1168":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#model_lab","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1169":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#try_feature","content":"Retrain the lab's picked model with `idea` added, on the same split: \\{verdict, text, series}. Keep it by\npassing features=\\{idea.id: result\\[\"series\"]} to the next model_lab."},"1170":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/lab","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/lab#try_feature","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1171":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","type":"page","content":"In-database training","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train"},"1172":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","content":"Prepare the ML Engineer's in-database training from an approved, fresh handoff (ML-3, design 7)."},"1173":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#prepare_training","content":"nb.prepare_training"},"1174":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"nb.TrainingPlan"},"1175":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","content":"Determinism (AC-ML3.4): the plan is a pure function of the handoff and the options - the features keep the handoff's\norder (the input schema, which the feature view fixes), a constant feature is dropped by a MIN/MAX query whose answer\ndepends on the data alone, and the rendered UDF trains `LogisticRegression(random_state=seed, solver=\"lbfgs\")` over\nrows it sorts first - so the same handoff, seed and data give the same metrics and the same coefficients."},"1176":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#prepare_training","content":"Refuse stale input, create the view, drop constant features and render the UDF and training SELECT."},"1177":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#prepare_training","content":"The caller creates `create_script` then passes `training_sql` to exasol_mlflow\\.start_run().\n`container` is the alias of the Python container the UDF runs on (the notebook's CONTAINER); None resolves it\nwith udf_container() - PYTHON3_ML before PYTHON3 from the kit's manifest, EXAKIT_UDF_CONTAINER first - and raises\nwith the fix when none is installed, before anything is written. `model_dir` is accepted for the earlier\nsignature; the model comes back through the query, in parts of up to 1 MB when it is bigger - no bucket is written. `class_weight` is None or \"balanced\",\npassed to logistic regression and recorded in the plan; it never changes the holdout split."},"1178":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#prepare_training","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/01_train`"},"1179":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"What in-database training will run, prepared from an approved, fresh handoff: the feature view and its columns, the\nscript that creates the training UDF, the training SQL and its parameters."},"1180":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"Member"},"1181":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"What it is"},"1182":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`view`"},"1183":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`str`"},"1184":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`features`"},"1185":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`tuple[str, ...]`"},"1186":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`create_script`"},"1187":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`str`"},"1188":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`training_sql`"},"1189":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`str`"},"1190":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`params`"},"1191":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`dict[str, Any]`"},"1192":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`handoff`"},"1193":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/ml-train#TrainingPlan","content":"`dict[str, Any]`"},"1194":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","type":"page","content":"Your own file or table","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file"},"1195":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","content":"Your own CSV, Parquet or JSON file as a dataset: loaded into a table over the kit's connection, described by a few role assignments, and checked by the same rules as a kit dataset - so the notebooks run on it unchanged."},"1196":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#load_own_file","content":"nb.load_own_file"},"1197":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"nb.LoadedTable"},"1198":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#save_descriptor","content":"nb.save_descriptor"},"1199":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#use_table","content":"nb.use_table"},"1200":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","content":"The descriptor is that mapping of role to column, a descriptor mapping (`schema_version`, `id`, `fact_table`,\n`roles`), or a descriptor file - YAML or JSON; `data/datasets/<id>/descriptor.yaml` in the kit shows the shape -\nwhose fact_table then names the table (`table` may be None). Given as a mapping of roles, they become a\nschema_version 2 \\*\\*draft\\*\\* (version 1, drafted by the user, owned by EXAKIT_DESCRIPTOR_OWNER or the OS user, its\n`source` the file) and are written beside the file as `<name>.descriptor.yaml` (when no descriptor is there yet),\nso `DATASET = \"<the file>\"` in a notebook opens it again with that one assignment; approving it (the quickstart's\napprove(), or exakit describe \\<id> --approve) is what the training and question steps wait for, exploring does not.\nThe rows travel over pyexasol's import on the open connection: no\nhost, user or password here, as everywhere in exakit.nb. Column types come from the file; the date role's column\nbecomes a DATE and a true/false column 0 or 1; a JSON file is an array of records or one record per line, its nested\nvalues kept as JSON text. The table is marked as loaded from the file (its comment holds the file's SHA-256), so\nrunning the cell again loads nothing when the file is unchanged and reloads it when it changed; a table of the same\nname that this did not create is refused unless `replace=True`."},"1201":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#load_own_file","content":"Load your own data and return it as a Dataset the notebooks run on (or a LoadedTable whose roles are reviewed\nnext). `path` is a CSV, Parquet or JSON file, or a folder of them (loaded by `exakit data-load`, exapump, one\ntable per file). `table` is the schema the tables go into (empty: the folder's name), each named after its file; or\nSCHEMA.TABLE to name the file's table, or the folder's table to describe next.\n`descriptor` (a file only) maps each role to a column of the file (`text` may name several), or is a\ndescriptor mapping or file (YAML or JSON; its fact_table names the table when `table` is None). `conn`\ndefaults to a new exakit.nb.connect(). With `missing_ok`, a path that is not there says so in one line and\nreturns None."},"1202":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"A file that has been loaded but has not yet received an approved descriptor."},"1203":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"Member"},"1204":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"What it is"},"1205":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"`id`"},"1206":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"`str`"},"1207":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"`fact_table`"},"1208":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"`str`"},"1209":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"`path`"},"1210":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#LoadedTable","content":"`Path`"},"1211":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#save_descriptor","content":"Write a descriptor document as YAML, in the layout of the kit's own descriptor.yaml files - always as\nschema_version 2: a schema_version 1 document (or one without the record keys) is written as version 1 with\n`status` (draft unless the document, or `status`, says approved), the owner (EXAKIT_DESCRIPTOR_OWNER, else the\nOS user), created now, drafted by the user and, when given, `source` (`file:<path>` for a file's descriptor).\nWhat the document already records is kept as it is."},"1212":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/own-file#use_table","content":"A table already in the database, to describe next (review_roles): `SCHEMA.TABLE`. A table whose columns kept\ntheir file's names (\"Won\", \"Opportunity ID\") cannot be read by unquoted queries, so it gets a view with plain\nnames over it in the prepared schema, said in one line; the table itself is never changed."},"1213":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","type":"page","content":"Typed view","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare"},"1214":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","content":"Prepare, the part that changes something: a typed, cleaned view of a table, proposed from the data and created only when the user says so."},"1215":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#typed_view","content":"nb.typed_view"},"1216":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"nb.TypedView"},"1217":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","content":"A file loaded as text (every column VARCHAR, as CSVs often are), blank cells, placeholder values and rows copied twice\nall make a result quietly wrong. typed_view() reads the table - not just its names - and proposes one view over it:"},"1218":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","content":"Nothing is written until `create()`: the proposal shows each change with the evidence for it and the exact SQL. Then\nthe view goes into the EXAKIT_PREPARED schema, and it gets its own approved descriptor - the same roles as the table it\ncame from, a column that became a date filling an empty time slot - so every later step reads the prepared data."},"1219":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#typed_view","content":"The proposal for `ds`'s table: its types, its cleaning and the CREATE VIEW, built from the data and the\ndescriptor. Only SELECTs run; nothing is created until `create()`."},"1220":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#typed_view","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1221":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"The proposal. `changes` and `cleaning` say what the view does differently from the table, `sql` is the\nCREATE VIEW that `create()` runs - nothing has run before that."},"1222":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"Member"},"1223":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"What it is"},"1224":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`dataset`"},"1225":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`Any`"},"1226":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`view`"},"1227":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`str`"},"1228":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`sql`"},"1229":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`str`"},"1230":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`changes`"},"1231":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`list[Change]`"},"1232":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`cleaning`"},"1233":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`list[str]`"},"1234":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`created`"},"1235":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`Any`"},"1236":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`needed`"},"1237":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"Whether the view would differ from the table at all."},"1238":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"`create(conn) -> Any`"},"1239":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/prepare#TypedView","content":"Create the view (after the user has read it), describe it, carry the table's roles over and approve them; returns the view's dataset, which the later steps then use."},"1240":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","type":"page","content":"Draft SQL without a model","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules"},"1241":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","content":"Draft Exasol SQL from a plain-language question, without an AI model: nb.draft_question."},"1242":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules#draft_question","content":"nb.draft_question"},"1243":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules#example_questions","content":"nb.example_questions"},"1244":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","content":"It matches common question shapes (rate, count, total, average per group; top N; trend over time; filters by year\nand by a group's value) to SQL templates over the approved column map, checks the SQL is read-only, and hands it to\nnb.ask(proposed_sql=...), so approval, logging and running are the kit's. `example_questions(dataset)` suggests\nquestions this dataset's roles can answer. Nothing leaves the computer: no model is called."},"1245":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules#draft_question","content":"A Proposal for `question` drafted by rules from the column map (no AI model): read-only SQL, with the\ndrafter's assumptions, not approved yet. Approve and run it as any proposal."},"1246":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules#draft_question","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"1247":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules#example_questions","content":"Up to three questions this dataset's approved roles can answer, in its own column names."},"1248":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/question-rules#example_questions","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"1249":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","type":"page","content":"Quickstart steps","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart"},"1250":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","content":"The steps both quickstarts share (notebook/notebooks/00_shared): is the database there, what does it hold, and one loader per way data comes in - a sample dataset the kit ships, your own file, an external source connected as a virtual schema."},"1251":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#check_connection","content":"nb.check_connection"},"1252":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#connected_sources","content":"nb.connected_sources"},"1253":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#first","content":"nb.first"},"1254":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#list_schemas","content":"nb.list_schemas"},"1255":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#load_sample","content":"nb.load_sample"},"1256":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#load_source","content":"nb.load_source"},"1257":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#show_roles","content":"nb.show_roles"},"1258":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","content":"The steps both quickstarts share (notebook/notebooks/00_shared): is the database there, what does it hold, and one\nloader per way data comes in - a sample dataset the kit ships, your own file, an external source connected as a\nvirtual schema. Each loader is one cell's call; one that is not set up says so in one line and returns None, so a\nnotebook runs top to bottom whichever ways the user picked."},"1259":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","content":"Nothing here prints a host, a user or a password."},"1260":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#check_connection","content":"The database answers: its time, this session's id and its version, as one row (and one line)."},"1261":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#connected_sources","content":"The virtual schemas in the database (external sources) with their number of tables; empty when there is none."},"1262":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#first","content":"The first dataset that was loaded, in the order given; says which one is used."},"1263":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#list_schemas","content":"Every schema with its number of tables, virtual ones (connected sources) marked."},"1264":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#load_sample","content":"A dataset the kit offers (`amazon_sales`, `fraud_transactions`): used as it is when it is loaded, else loaded\nfirst with `exakit data-load <id>` (the cell waits for it), then checked against the database. None skips it."},"1265":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#load_source","content":"A table in a connected external source (a virtual schema). `descriptor` is `VS_<NAME>.<TABLE>` (any case,\nthe VS\\_ prefix optional), `VS_<NAME>` alone (its one table, or a list of them), or a descriptor file whose\nfact_table is in a source. None skips it and lists the sources there are. A name that cannot be used stops the\ncell with one line naming what is there and how to connect one; the table is read once (one row) to prove it."},"1266":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#show_roles","content":"The descriptor's roles, one per line, as the notebook will use them."},"1267":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/quickstart#show_roles","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`"},"1268":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","type":"page","content":"Plain-language notes","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout"},"1269":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","content":"Plain-language notes under a notebook's results, for a reader who is not a data scientist."},"1270":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#count_name","content":"nb.count_name"},"1271":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#name","content":"nb.name"},"1272":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_groups","content":"nb.note_groups"},"1273":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_model","content":"nb.note_model"},"1274":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_trend","content":"nb.note_trend"},"1275":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#noun","content":"nb.noun"},"1276":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","content":"Each note says what one row of the result is, what each number means in the data's own words (`ds.grain`: \"one\nrow per order line\" makes them order lines), the overall figure, the highest and lowest groups, which groups are too small to\ntrust, and that a difference between groups is not a cause. Nothing is computed that the result does not hold."},"1277":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#count_name","content":"The count column, named after what is counted: ORDER_LINES, STORE_WEEKS; ROW_COUNT when the descriptor does\nnot say (ROWS is an SQL word)."},"1278":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#count_name","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"1279":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#name","content":"A result column named after a data column: `CANCELLED` + `PCT` -> `CANCELLED_PCT`; quotes, dots and\nspaces become underscores, so the name works unquoted in SQL."},"1280":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#name","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"1281":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_groups","content":"Print (and return) the note under a per-group result: one line per fact, in the data's own words."},"1282":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_groups","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `data-scientist/01_explore`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"1283":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_model","content":"Print (and return) the note under the small model's score, in words."},"1284":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_model","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1285":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_trend","content":"Print (and return) the note under a per-period result: the busiest period and the highest and lowest %."},"1286":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#note_trend","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1287":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/readout","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/readout#noun","content":"What a row is, from the descriptor's grain: \"one row per order line\" -> \"order lines\" (`one=True`: \"order\nline\"), \"one row per store and week\" -> \"store weeks\"; at most three words, up to a comma or a word such as \"in\" or\n\"per\"; \"rows\" when the descriptor does not say."},"1288":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","type":"page","content":"Review and approve roles","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker"},"1289":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","content":"Review the profiler's proposed roles in a notebook and approve a versioned descriptor (DS-5, design 2.2)."},"1290":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#review_roles","content":"nb.review_roles"},"1291":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"nb.RoleReview"},"1292":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","content":"The picker is the descriptor itself: one dropdown per column with the eight roles (key, time, measure, category, flag,\ntext, identifier, other), set to the role the rules drafted and labelled with the evidence that chose it; then one\ndropdown per slot - the columns the notebooks use (key, time, text, target, category, entity) - set to the drafted\ncolumn; then an Approve button. In JupyterLab it is\nipywidgets; in Marimo the review itself is a `mo.ui.dictionary` of `mo.ui.dropdown` with a `mo.ui.run_button`, so\n`ds = review.dataset()` runs again when the button is clicked and stops cleanly (`mo.stop`) until then; in a plain\nPython session `review.approve({\"COLUMN\": \"role\", ...})` is the same path."},"1293":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","content":"Headless (`EXAKIT_NB_AUTO_APPROVE`, set by `tools/notebooks.py --run`): `1` approves the proposal only when its\nroles equal the current approved version's (the kit's store, else the shipped descriptor) - then nothing is written,\nno new version, no column comments, so a CI run is idempotent; a proposal that differs stays a draft, the run says\nwhy, and `dataset()` hands the draft on so a step that needs an approval (`require_approved`) says what to do.\n`force` approves whatever was proposed: a deliberately scripted approval."},"1294":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","content":"`review_roles(conn, name)` with a notebook's one assignment (a dataset id, a descriptor file, a data file) opens it as\nit is described; a data file with no descriptor beside it is loaded, profiled and reviewed right there, the draft\nsaved beside it so the assignment reopens it. The active workflow's log gets `describe.draft` and\n`describe.approve` lines (X-1)."},"1295":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#review_roles","content":"Profile the loaded sample, file or connected table, show evidence and role choices, then await approval. Given\na name (a notebook's one assignment: a dataset id, a descriptor file, a data file with its roles beside it) the\ndataset is opened as it is described and nothing is profiled; a data file with no descriptor beside it is loaded\nand reviewed here."},"1296":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#review_roles","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1297":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"One proposal. Jupyter shows a dropdown per column and an Approve button; elsewhere approve(choices) is the same\npath. dataset() stops the next cell until approval happened (a headless run hands the draft on, see the module)."},"1298":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"Member"},"1299":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"What it is"},"1300":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"`suggestions() -> dict[str, str]`"},"1301":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"\\{column: drafted role} (one of the eight), in table order."},"1302":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"`low_confidence() -> list[str]`"},"1303":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"The columns drafted at low confidence, in table order: where the draft guessed, so a person looks first."},"1304":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"`review_order() -> list[str]`"},"1305":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"The columns as the pickers show them: low confidence first, then the rest, each in table order."},"1306":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker#RoleReview","content":"`slot_suggestions() -> dict[str, str \\| None]`"},"1307":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/role-picker","tags":[],"type":"text",