ence/schema-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#describe_schema","content":"nb.describe_schema"},"1329":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#JoinedView","content":"nb.JoinedView"},"1330":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#SchemaMap","content":"nb.SchemaMap"},"1331":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","content":"A table's column map says what its columns are; the schema map says how the schema's tables fit together - every\ntable with its rows and key, and every many-to-one link between them, declared by the database or found (a column\nthat names another table's key and whose every value is in it), each with its evidence. The kit's describe service\ndoes the work (setup/lib/descriptor/schema.py); this module shows it in a notebook and turns it into a dataset:"},"1332":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","content":"Nothing is written before create(): the proposal shows every join and the exact SQL. Then the schema map is approved\n(its links published as EXAKIT_SEMANTIC.\\<SCHEMA>\\_\\_RELATIONS for agents), the view goes into EXAKIT_PREPARED and gets\nits own approved column map - the main table's roles carried over - so every later step reads the joined data."},"1333":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#describe_schema","content":"The schema of `dataset_or_schema` (a dataset, or a schema name) as found now: its tables, rows and keys, and\nevery many-to-one link between them with its evidence. A live source's schema is not surveyed (its tables are\nqueried in place, every count a round trip)."},"1334":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#describe_schema","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1335":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#JoinedView","content":"The proposal for one wide view. `joins` lists each table it adds and how; `sql` is what create() runs."},"1336":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#JoinedView","content":"Member"},"1337":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#JoinedView","content":"What it is"},"1338":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#JoinedView","content":"`schema_map`"},"1339":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#JoinedView","content":"`SchemaMap`"},"1340":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#JoinedView","content":"`view`"},"1341":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/schema-map#JoinedView","content":"\\`str"},"1342":{"id":