-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"The catalog's line under the title: the approved data it answers from."},"1433":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"`preview(tool: Tool, profile_name: str='starter-kit', windows: bool \\| None=None) -> str`"},"1434":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"Create and health-check a preview; on Windows use build + healthcheck."},"1435":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"`confirm(tool: Tool, figures_checked: bool=False) -> str`"},"1436":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/share-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/share","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/share#ShareDraft","content":"Promote the exact healthy preview after a human checks its figures."},"1437":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"page","content":"External sources","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources"},"1438":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","content":"External sources from a notebook cell: connect one, and read what a cell was given."},"1439":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#clean_path","content":"nb.clean_path"},"1440":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#connect_source","content":"nb.connect_source"},"1441":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#read_connection_string","content":"nb.read_connection_string"},"1442":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#source_engine","content":"nb.source_engine"},"1443":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceProblem","content":"nb.SourceProblem"},"1444":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"nb.SourceTest"},"1445":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#test_source","content":"nb.test_source"},"1446":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","content":"connect_source runs `exakit connect <connector> --name <name> ... --password-stdin --yes --json`. The password is\nasked in a hidden box and goes to the command on standard input: never into the cell, the command line or a log."},"1447":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#clean_path","content":"A path pasted into a cell, made usable: quotes and spaces around it, a `file://` link, the shell's\nbackslash escapes (`My\\ Data`, from a drag into a terminal) and `~` are undone. Empty stays empty."},"1448":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#connect_source","content":"Connect an external source as a virtual schema, from a notebook cell. `connector` is the kit's id or alias\n(`postgresql`, `pg`, `mysql`, `snowflake` ...; `exakit help connect` lists them), `name` becomes the\nschema `VS_<NAME>`. Give the source's connection string as `url` (a JDBC URL, `postgres://...`), or each\ninput as a keyword (`host=`, `database=`, `schema=`, `user=` ...; the connector's skill lists them).\nThe password is asked in a hidden box (Enter: none), or read from `password_file`; a password inside `url` is\ntaken out of it and used, never shown. Marimo has no hidden prompt: pass a password field as `password`\n(`mo.ui.text(kind=\"password\")`, its value is read) or a `password_file`. `dry_run` checks the inputs and\nconnects nothing. A connector with several kinds of source in one takes its settings as keywords too\n(`catalog=\"unity\", files=\"s3\"` for a Lakehouse; nb.connector_inputs lists them). A source with a second secret\n(a Lakehouse catalog login plus storage keys) takes it as `storage_secret_file`, or as `storage_secret` (the\ntext, a Marimo password field, or a function that asks for it): it reaches the kit in a file only this user can\nread, removed as soon as the kit has read it. Returns the schema name (`VS_SALES`) when connected, None for a dry run; raises SourceProblem with the kit's reason otherwise."},"1449":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#read_connection_string","content":"Read a source's connection string exactly as `exakit connect --url` does: it is handed to the kit's engine\n(its `paste` command, on standard input, never as an argument). Returns \\{connector, values, notes, dropped,\nmasked, credential_in_string, secret_input, missing}: `values` by input name, each checked as if typed;\n`masked` the string with every credential as \\*\\*\\*\\*; `missing` the connector's required inputs the string does\nnot give (and no default covers). The string's password is used by nb.connect_source(url=...) and is never\nreturned, printed or logged here. For a connector with settings (a Lakehouse's `catalog=`, `files=`) give the\nones already chosen: a setting the string itself shows (an s3:// path\nis a folder with no catalog) comes back in `values`, and `missing` is what that combination still needs."},"1450":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#source_engine","content":"Ask the kit's own source engine (setup/virtual-schemas/engine/cli.py, the coordinator behind `exakit connect`\nand `exakit source`) one of the questions its connect form asks, and return its --json answer:"},"1451":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#source_engine","content":"Run as the kit's shell runs it: the kit's Python where it is installed, isolated (-I), with this installation's\ndefinitions and home. None of these four touches the database. A refusal is a SourceProblem in the engine's\nwords, with its remedy."},"1452":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceProblem","content":"A source cell that cannot go on, said in one short message: no traceback in a notebook."},"1453":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"What test_source found, one check per line: (what was checked, passed, what it said)."},"1454":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"Member"},"1455":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"What it is"},"1456":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`connector`"},"1457":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`str`"},"1458":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`name`"},"1459":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`str`"},"1460":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`checks`"},"1461":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`list[tuple[str, bool, str]]`"},"1462":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#SourceTest","content":"`ok`"},"1463":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/sources","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/sources#test_source","content":"Test a source before connecting it, changing nothing: first the kit's own check of every input\n(`exakit connect ... --dry-run`), then whether this computer reaches the source's host and port. No password is\nneeded or sent. The sign-in itself is checked by nb.connect_source, from the database (exakit source check)."},"1464":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","type":"page","content":"Themes in text (AI)","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes"},"1465":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","content":"What the texts on each side of the label are about, read by your model and traced to your Langfuse."},"1466":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes#themes","content":"nb.themes"},"1467":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","content":"One model call per side (label = 1, label = 0): the model sorts that side's texts into two to four themes\nand answers in JSON, so the result is a table - theme, how many texts, their share, an example - with a note in plain\nwords under it. A theme found on one side only is the clue: what those texts are about that the others are not."},"1468":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","content":"With Langfuse set up (nb.trace), both calls are one trace, `explore-themes`, each call named after its side, with\nwhat was sent, the answer, tokens, cost and time, and two scores to compare models and runs by: `valid_json` (1 when\nevery answer could be read) and `texts_placed` (the share of texts the model gave a theme)."},"1469":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes#themes","content":"Sort each side's texts into themes with `endpoint` = (client, model) from nb.model_client(); return the table\n(a pandas DataFrame when pandas is there, else a list of rows) and print the note. None without an endpoint."},"1470":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/themes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/themes#themes","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`"},"1471":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"page","content":"Workflows","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Command reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow"},"1472":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"One workflow id on everything (X-1): workflow() starts or resumes one, and every helper that does something appends a line to its log while it is active - a statement, a trace, an MLflow run, a descriptor draft or approval, a handoff, a dashboard revision, a model put."},"1473":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#continue_workflow","content":"nb.continue_workflow"},"1474":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#current_workflow","content":"nb.current_workflow"},"1475":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#last_workflow","content":"nb.last_workflow"},"1476":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#list_workflows","content":"nb.list_workflows"},"1477":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_event","content":"nb.log_event"},"1478":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_sql","content":"nb.log_sql"},"1479":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow","content":"nb.workflow"},"1480":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow_log","content":"nb.workflow_log"},"1481":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"One workflow id on everything (X-1): `workflow()` starts or resumes one, and every helper that does something\nappends a line to its log while it is active - a statement, a trace, an MLflow run, a descriptor draft or approval, a\nhandoff, a dashboard revision, a model put. Without a workflow nothing is written: there are no implicit workflows."},"1482":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"A notebook never needs an id pasted in: the quickstart starts the work and every later notebook continues it with\n`continue_workflow`, which takes this kernel's workflow, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else the\nlast one started or resumed on this machine ($EXAKIT_HOME/last-workflow), and starts a new one only when there is none."},"1483":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"The id is `wf-YYYYMMDD-<6 hex>`, kept in the session store and in EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID so a child process (a CLI call\nfrom a notebook) inherits it. The log is `$EXAKIT_HOME/workflows/<id>.jsonl` (EXAKIT_HOME default\n\\~/.exasol-starter-kit), append-only, one JSON object per line: `{ts, workflow_id, kind, ...payload}`; the folder is\n0700 and the file 0600, each line one O_APPEND write so two kernels on one workflow never interleave. A log that\ncannot be written warns and the cell goes on: logging never fails the work it describes."},"1484":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"Credential-shaped payload keys are checked recursively, including JSON-encoded metadata strings. A secret-named key\nor a DSN containing a password is refused (a\nValueError - the caller's mistake, before anything is written). SQL text is screened rather than refused: a statement\nthat mentions PASSWORD, API_KEY, IDENTIFIED BY and the like - or carries a DSN with a password - is logged with its\ntext replaced by `<redacted: credential-like SQL>` and `redacted: true`, its digest kept, and one warning; the\nlogger never fails the query it records, which has already run. Other SQL text is kept so the user can find the\nquery again."},"1485":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","content":"`python -m exakit_nb.workflow list|show <id> [--json]` is what `exakit workflow` runs."},"1486":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#continue_workflow","content":"The workflow already going, without an id to paste: this kernel's, else the one inherited through\nEXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else the last one started or resumed on this machine (a quickstart starts one); a new one named\n`name` only when there is none. Says which, and returns the id. The first time a notebook continues a\nworkflow the log gets one `step` line with `name`, so the kit can tell which notebooks took part."},"1487":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#continue_workflow","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/01_explore`, `data-scientist/02_ask_your_data`, `data-scientist/03_share`, `ml-engineer/01_train`, `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`"},"1488":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#current_workflow","content":"The active workflow id: the session's, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else None."},"1489":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#current_workflow","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`"},"1490":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#last_workflow","content":"The workflow started or resumed last on this machine, when its log is still there; else None."},"1491":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#list_workflows","content":"One summary per log in the workflows folder, oldest first: id, name (from its start line), started, last\n(first and last timestamps) and events (the line count). An unreadable log is skipped."},"1492":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#list_workflows","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1493":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_event","content":"Append one line to the active workflow's log; nothing when no workflow is active. A credential-named payload\nkey or a DSN with a password is a ValueError (the caller's mistake); credential-like statement text is logged\nredacted with a warning (never an exception: the statement already ran); a log that cannot be written is a warning\n(the environment's)."},"1494":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_event","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/02_rust_score`"},"1495":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_sql","content":"Log a statement sql() ran: the session and statement ids that find it in the database's audit log, the\nstatement's SHA-256 (what traces and runs carry), how many rows came back, and the statement text - redacted, with\na warning, when it looks credential-bearing (a PASSWORD or API_KEY column, say); this never raises, the query has\nalready run. No-op without a workflow; the statement id is looked up on the connection unless given."},"1496":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#log_sql","content":"**Used in:** `ml-engineer/01_train`"},"1497":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow","content":"Start a workflow (a new id, a `start` line in its log) or, with `resume`, continue an existing one. The id\nbecomes the session's and EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID's, and is returned. Resuming an id whose log does not exist is a\nValueError naming the path, so a typo never starts an empty log under a made-up id."},"1498":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`, `ml-engineer/00_quickstart`"},"1499":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow_log","content":"Every line of a workflow's log, in order. A missing log is a FileNotFoundError naming the path."},"1500":{"id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/reference/workflow#workflow_log","content":"**Used in:** `data-scientist/00_quickstart`"},"1501":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"page","content":"Guided and Code","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Start here"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code"},"1502":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","content":"The cards each notebook opens with, the Code switch, and how a button and a cell are the same call."},"1503":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"The guided view"},"1504":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-docs-button","content":"The Docs button"},"1505":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"The Code switch"},"1506":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-call-two-ways","content":"One call, two ways"},"1507":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-home-card","content":"The Home card"},"1508":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-workflow-per-start","content":"One workflow per start"},"1509":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"Each Data Scientist notebook opens with cards that do the page's steps with buttons and forms."},"1510":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"Notebook"},"1511":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"Its cards open with"},"1512":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`00_quickstart`"},"1513":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`guide.start()`"},"1514":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`01_explore`"},"1515":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`guide.explore()`"},"1516":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`02_ask_your_data`"},"1517":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`guide.ask()`"},"1518":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`03_share`"},"1519":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-guided-view","content":"`guide.share()`"},"1520":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-docs-button","content":"The first card of every notebook has a **Docs** button beside the logo. It opens this documentation in a new tab, on the guide for that notebook: loading data from the quickstart, exploring from `01_explore`, asking from `02_ask_your_data`, sharing from `03_share`."},"1521":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"Every card has a **Guided / Code** switch at its top right."},"1522":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"**Code** turns that card, in place, into its code as cells: what it ran this session, in order, and the exact call behind each control. Each cell can be edited and run right there with **Run** or Shift+Enter, and shows what it printed or returned under it, like a notebook cell. It runs in the notebook's own session, so it sees the same connection and data as the cards. **Copy as cell** copies it into a cell of your own, and **Reset** puts the original back."},"1523":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"**Guided** turns it back. Only that card changes. The connection, the chosen data and the approvals stay as they are."},"1524":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-code-switch","content":"The notebook's own cells sit under **The code behind this page**. In the kit's JupyterLab they are hidden until you choose **Show all the notebook's code cells** at the foot of a card's Code view. In Marimo the cards show stacked, and the cells open with their code visible."},"1525":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-call-two-ways","content":"Every button, form and choice on a card is one `exakit.nb` call, and the same call is a cell in the notebook's code section. Clicking **Approve** and running `role_review.approve(...)` do the same thing."},"1526":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-call-two-ways","content":"What a card shows is read from the kit when it draws: the datasets, connectors, add-ons and notebooks are not written into the card. A connector added to the kit appears in the form with no notebook change."},"1527":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-home-card","content":"The first card of the quickstart is the kit itself. It has two tabs."},"1528":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-home-card","content":"**Your kit:** what is installed and running, the loaded datasets, your approved column maps and your workflows."},"1529":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#the-home-card","content":"**Marketplace:** every add-on with **Install**, **Start** and **Update** buttons. They run `nb.addon_ready(id)` and `nb.kit_update(id)`, which is what `exakit marketplace` and `exakit update` do in a terminal."},"1530":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/guided-and-code#one-workflow-per-start","content":"`guide.start()` starts a workflow. Every card action after it is one line in that workflow's log: the card, the action, the code it ran and whether it worked. See Workflows."},"1531":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"page","content":"The notebooks and the nine steps","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Data Scientist","Start here"],"tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks"},"1532":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-0","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","content":"What each of the four Data Scientist notebooks does, in order, and how to open them."},"1533":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-1","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#open-the-notebooks","content":"Open the notebooks"},"1534":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-2","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"The path"},"1535":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-3","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-nine-steps","content":"The nine steps"},"1536":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-4","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#access","content":"Access"},"1537":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-5","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#understand","content":"Understand"},"1538":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-6","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#prepare","content":"Prepare"},"1539":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-7","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#explore","content":"Explore"},"1540":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-8","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#model","content":"Model"},"1541":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-9","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#validate","content":"Validate"},"1542":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-10","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#ask-with-ai","content":"Ask with AI"},"1543":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-11","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#share","content":"Share"},"1544":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-12","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#hand-off","content":"Hand off"},"1545":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-13","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#rules-every-notebook-follows","content":"Rules every notebook follows"},"1546":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-14","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#open-the-notebooks","content":"Both open in your browser on the kit's own Python, with the kernel **Exasol (Starter Kit)**. That kernel knows where the kit's connection is, so no notebook asks for a host, a user or a password."},"1547":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-15","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#open-the-notebooks","content":"Your copies are in `~/.exasol-starter-kit/notebooks/starter-kit-notebooks/data-scientist/`. A notebook you edited is never overwritten by an update."},"1548":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-16","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"Run the notebooks in order. Each one continues the workflow the first one started, so you paste no id and copy nothing between them."},"1549":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-17","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"Notebook"},"1550":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-18","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"Steps"},"1551":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-19","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"What you have at the end"},"1552":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-20","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"`00_quickstart`"},"1553":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-21","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"0 Check the kit, 1 Access, 2 Understand"},"1554":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-22","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"A connection, a loaded dataset and an approved column map"},"1555":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-23","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"`01_explore`"},"1556":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-24","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"3 Prepare, 4 Explore, 5 Model, 6 Validate"},"1557":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-25","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"Clean data, comparisons by group and over time, a small model and its score"},"1558":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-26","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"`02_ask_your_data`"},"1559":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-27","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"7 Ask with AI"},"1560":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-28","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"An answer from SQL you read and approved"},"1561":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-29","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"`03_share`"},"1562":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-30","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"8 Share, 9 Hand off"},"1563":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-31","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#the-path","content":"A published dashboard and one folder a colleague can repeat the work from"},"1564":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-32","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#access","content":"Connect, start a workflow and load data: a kit dataset, your own file, or an external source. See Load data."},"1565":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-33","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#understand","content":"Approve the column map: which column is the key, the time, the text, the target (the outcome to predict), the category and the entity. See Column map and approval."},"1566":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-34","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#prepare","content":"Check the data is clean, see the tables linked to it, and optionally create a typed, cleaned view. See Prepared views."},"1567":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-35","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#explore","content":"Compare groups and look at the data over time. Each query shows its SQL before its result."},"1568":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-36","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#model","content":"Set aside columns that give the answer away, then train a small baseline model."},"1569":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-37","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#validate","content":"Score the model on rows it has not seen and see what it leans on."},"1570":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-38","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#ask-with-ai","content":"Ask in plain language, read the proposed SQL, approve it, run it read-only. See Ask your data."},"1571":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-39","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#share","content":"Turn one checked result into a dashboard: a preview first, published after you check the figures. See Share a dashboard."},"1572":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-40","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#hand-off","content":"Pack the column map, every query, the dashboards and the workflow log into one folder and a zip."},"1573":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-41","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#hand-off","content":"Step 0, at the top of the quickstart, checks the kit itself from the notebook. See Run the kit from a notebook."},"1574":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-42","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#rules-every-notebook-follows","content":"**One assignment picks the data.** `SAMPLE = \"...\"` in the quickstart, `DATASET = \"...\"` in the others. `None` means the dataset approved last."},"1575":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-43","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#rules-every-notebook-follows","content":"**No column name is typed.** Queries are built from the approved roles, so the same notebook runs on any table."},"1576":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-44","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#rules-every-notebook-follows","content":"**AI is opt-in.** The AI steps stay off until you turn them on, and a model never approves roles."},"1577":{"id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks-45","page_id":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/data-scientist/start/notebooks#rules-every-notebook-follows","content":"**A step that cannot run says why.** A dataset with no text column skips the text steps and tells you."},"1578":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"page","content":"Column maps","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","All personas","Data"],"tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps"},"1579":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-0","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps","content":"Say what each column of a table means with exakit describe - draft, correct, approve, and see every version."},"1580":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-1","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#draft","content":"Draft"},"1581":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-2","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#approve","content":"Approve"},"1582":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-3","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"What you get at the end"},"1583":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-4","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#see-and-compare","content":"See and compare"},"1584":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-5","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#a-whole-schema","content":"A whole schema"},"1585":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-6","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#where-they-are-kept","content":"Where they are kept"},"1586":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-7","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#when-the-table-changes","content":"When the table changes"},"1587":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-8","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#with-an-ai-model","content":"With an AI model"},"1588":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-9","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/column-maps#from-a-notebook","content":"From a notebook"},"1589":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-10","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps","content":"A **column map** (the descriptor) gives every column of a table a role. Notebooks and AI clients read it, so they all work from the same meaning. For the idea behind it, see Column map and approval."},"1590":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-11","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#draft","content":"The table is profiled with SELECTs only. Nothing is written to the database. Every column gets one of eight roles, with its confidence and the evidence that chose it:"},"1591":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-12","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#draft","content":"`key`, `time`, `measure`, `category`, `flag`, `text`, `identifier`, `other`."},"1592":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-13","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#draft","content":"The draft is deterministic: the same table gives the same draft."},"1593":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-14","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#draft","content":"A column whose values look like e-mail addresses, phone numbers, IBANs or postcodes is marked **sensitive**."},"1594":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-15","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#draft","content":"The **target** is never drafted. Only a person sets it."},"1595":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-16","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#approve","content":"`--role <slot>=<COLUMN>` corrects a slot: `key`, `time`, `text`, `target`, `category`, `entity`. `<slot>=-` leaves it empty."},"1596":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-17","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#approve","content":"Approval:"},"1597":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-18","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#approve","content":"checks that every column has a role, that none sits in two slots, and that the table has not changed since it was profiled"},"1598":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-19","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#approve","content":"writes a new version, never rewriting an old one"},"1599":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-20","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#approve","content":"publishes the roles as column comments on a view, `EXAKIT_SEMANTIC.<SCHEMA>__<TABLE>`, readable by the read-only AI user"},"1600":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-21","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#approve","content":"Your own table is never commented. If publishing fails, the approval still stands and the message says why."},"1601":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-22","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"A new version of the column map, kept under `~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/`, and the roles published on the view `EXAKIT_SEMANTIC.<SCHEMA>__<TABLE>`. The notebooks and AI clients read the approved version from then on."},"1602":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-23","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#see-and-compare","content":"Add `--json` to any of them for a script."},"1603":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-24","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#a-whole-schema","content":"This lists every table with its rows and key, and every many-to-one link between tables with its evidence. A link is a foreign key the database declares, or a column whose values are in another table's key (at most 0.1% of them may be missing). A name alone never makes a link."},"1604":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-25","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#a-whole-schema","content":"`--link TABLE.COLUMN=TABLE.KEY` adds a link and `--unlink TABLE.COLUMN` removes one. The approved links are published as the view `EXAKIT_SEMANTIC.<SCHEMA>__RELATIONS`."},"1605":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-26","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#where-they-are-kept","content":"`~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/<SCHEMA>.<TABLE>/`: the draft, every approved version and the current one."},"1606":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-27","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#when-the-table-changes","content":"Columns whose name and type did not change keep their approved roles. The rest are flagged, and you approve again."},"1607":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-28","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#with-an-ai-model","content":"When a model is set up, one call adds a one-line note per column. It is sent each column's name, type, role, evidence and top values, never a row and never a sensitive column. A note never decides a role."},"1608":{"id":"/kit/data/column-maps-29","page_id":"/kit/data/column-maps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/column-maps#from-a-notebook","content":"See Review and approve the column map."},"1609":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","type":"page","content":"Datasets","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","All personas","Data"],"tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/datasets"},"1610":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-0","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets","content":"The sample datasets the kit carries, where each comes from, and which persona loads it."},"1611":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-1","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/datasets#downloaded-datasets","content":"Downloaded datasets"},"1612":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-2","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/datasets#a-dataset-with-a-column-map","content":"A dataset with a column map"},"1613":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-3","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/datasets#load-one-again","content":"Load one again"},"1614":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-4","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/datasets#add-a-dataset-to-the-kit","content":"Add a dataset to the kit"},"16