ith the kit, loads without internet"},"1628":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-18","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets","content":"`amazon_sales`"},"1629":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-19","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets","content":"Data Scientist, ML Engineer"},"1630":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-20","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets","content":"Downloaded when you load it"},"1631":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-21","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets","content":"`fraud_transactions`"},"1632":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-22","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets","content":"Data Scientist, ML Engineer"},"1633":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-23","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets","content":"Downloaded when you load it"},"1634":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-24","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets#downloaded-datasets","content":"`amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions` are archives in the kit's datasets release. An archive is fetched only when you load that dataset. The kit checks the archive's SHA-256 and every file's digest, and refuses a mismatch."},"1635":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-25","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets#a-dataset-with-a-column-map","content":"`amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions` each ship with an approved column map, so the notebooks can use them straight away. You can approve your own version at any time."},"1636":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-26","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets#a-dataset-with-a-column-map","content":"The ML Engineer persona is not offered in this release, so for now only Data Scientist and General load these datasets."},"1637":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-27","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets#load-one-again","content":"`--force` drops that dataset's tables and rebuilds them. Anything you changed in its schema is lost."},"1638":{"id":"/kit/data/datasets-28","page_id":"/kit/data/datasets","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/datasets#add-a-dataset-to-the-kit","content":"A dataset is one folder in `data/datasets/`. Nothing else names it, so a new folder appears in the menu."},"1639":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","type":"page","content":"Load data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","All personas","Data"],"tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/load-data"},"1640":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-0","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data","content":"Load a kit dataset, one file or a whole folder with exakit data-load, and what happens when you run it again."},"1641":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-1","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/load-data#running-it-again-is-safe","content":"Running it again is safe"},"1642":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-2","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/load-data#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"What you get at the end"},"1643":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-3","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/load-data#from-a-notebook","content":"From a notebook"},"1644":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-4","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/load-data#an-external-source","content":"An external source"},"1645":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-5","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data","content":"On a terminal this opens a menu: the kit's datasets, your own data, or an external source. Name what you want to skip the menu."},"1646":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-6","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data","content":"See Datasets for the list."},"1647":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-7","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data","content":"It asks two things, whatever the file's kind: the file, then `SCHEMA.TABLE`. To answer up front:"},"1648":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-8","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data","content":"CSV, Parquet and JSON are loaded. JSON is split into tables by an engine the kit installs for you on macOS, Linux and WSL. A `;`-separated CSV is loaded with its delimiter. A tabular `.txt` or `.tsv` file is listed with the rename to `.csv` that the loader needs."},"1649":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-9","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data","content":"Every CSV, Parquet and JSON (.json, .geojson) file at the folder's top level becomes one table named after the file. The schema is asked once:"},"1650":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-10","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data","content":"Subfolders are not scanned. Files of other kinds are ignored. Duplicates are skipped with the reason. On Windows, a folder's JSON files are listed as skipped."},"1651":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-11","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data#running-it-again-is-safe","content":"A file already loaded is skipped, not loaded on top of itself."},"1652":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-12","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data#running-it-again-is-safe","content":"A file that a stopped run left half-written is loaded again from scratch."},"1653":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-13","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data#running-it-again-is-safe","content":"A table holding rows this kit did not load is left alone, unless you say otherwise."},"1654":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-14","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data#running-it-again-is-safe","content":"`EXAKIT_ON_EXISTING` takes `skip` (the default), `replace` or `append`. Without a terminal the answer is `skip`. On a terminal you are asked."},"1655":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-15","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data#what-you-get-at-the-end","content":"Every file is listed with its table and the rows that landed, or the reason it did not load. A file the loader refuses leaves no empty table behind."},"1656":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-16","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data#from-a-notebook","content":"See Load data in the Data Scientist notebooks."},"1657":{"id":"/kit/data/load-data-17","page_id":"/kit/data/load-data","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/load-data#an-external-source","content":"Data in another database is not copied. It is connected with `exakit connect` and read where it lives. See Sources."},"1658":{"id":"/kit/data/run-sql","page_id":"/kit/data/run-sql","type":"page","content":"Run SQL","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","All personas","Data"],"tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/run-sql"},"1659":{"id":"/kit/data/run-sql-0","page_id":"/kit/data/run-sql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/kit/data/run-sql","content":"Run one statement from the terminal with exakit sql, read-only unless you say otherwise."},"1660":{"id":"/kit/data/run-sql-1","page_id":"/kit/data/run-sql","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/run-sql#reads-only-unless-you-say-otherwise","content":"Reads only unless you say otherwise"},"1661":{"id":"/kit/data/run-sql-2","page_id":"/kit/data/run-sql","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/run-sql#a-saved-statement","content":"A saved statement"},"1662":{"id":"/kit/data/run-sql-3","page_id":"/kit/data/run-sql","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/kit/data/run-sql#errors-come-with-their-fix","content":"Errors come with their fix"},"1663":