S_<NAME>`"],[1625,"`weather`"],[797,"`what` is nothing (the section of the persona whose notebook this is, else the start page), a helper or its name (`nb.describe`, `\"describe\"`: that command's page),\na page's address (`\"concepts/descriptor\"`), or any other words (searched, typos forgiven). The result shows\nunder the cell in a frame `height` pixels tall; `browser=True` opens a browser tab too. Served from this\ncomputer only, from files the kit ships: nothing is fetched from the internet."],[814,"`workflow_id`"],[1417,"`workflow_id`"],[384,"`workflow.jsonl`"],[186,"`workflows/<id>.jsonl`"],[811,"`zip_path`"],[1553,"0 Check the kit, 1 Access, 2 Understand"],[1556,"3 Prepare, 4 Explore, 5 Model, 6 Validate"],[1559,"7 Ask with AI"],[1562,"8 Share, 9 Hand off"],[1589,"A **column map** (the descriptor) gives every column of a table a role. Notebooks and AI clients read it, so they all work from the same meaning. For the idea behind it, see Column map and approval."],[275,"A **column map** says what each column of a table is for. Its technical name is the **descriptor**, which is the word you see in code and in some file names. Every later query is built from the column map, so no notebook types your column names."],[249,"A **dataset** is a table in the database together with its approved column map. The notebooks never read a table directly. They read a dataset, and build every query from its roles."],[405,"A **Lakehouse** is one connector for several things: an Iceberg REST catalog, Unity Catalog, AWS Glue, or Parquet files in a plain folder, with the files on S3 or Azure. Two **settings** pick the combination, and each combination asks for different details."],[2018,"A **persona** is a named set of answers to the questions the installer asks: which datasets to load, which AI clients to connect and which add-ons to install. Choosing a persona is choosing what this computer is for."],[81,"A **persona** is the kit set up for one kind of work. It decides which datasets are loaded, which add-ons are installed and which notebooks you get. See What is a persona."],[1710,"A **skill** is a set of instructions that teaches an AI client how to use the kit: which command loads data, how to read a column map, where dashboards go."],[425,"A **workflow** gives one id to every query and decision in a piece of work. The quickstart starts it and the other notebooks continue it. You never paste an id."],[1767,"A button or form on a notebook card ran, with the code it ran and whether it worked"],[52,"A certificate cannot be verified"],[333,"A column map starts as a **draft**: the kit's proposal. A proposal can be wrong. In `amazon_sales`, `STATUS` gives the answer away; the kit warns about it and the model leaves it out."],[1755,"A column map was drafted or approved"],[361,"A column whose values almost decide the target on their own would make a model look better than it is. These columns are listed and left out of the model."],[1593,"A column whose values look like e-mail addresses, phone numbers, IBANs or postcodes is marked **sensitive**."],[505,"A command run from a cell has no terminal, so a question it would ask takes its default. Give a choice up front instead: `nb.exakit(\"mcp-setup\", env={\"EXAKIT_MCP_CLIENTS\": \"claude\"})`."],[790,"A command's page is found in the site's own list (`commands.json`, written from `exakit.nb`'s `__all__` when the\nsite is built), so every public helper has one. Anything else is handed to the site's search."],[1554,"A connection, a loaded dataset and an approved column map"],[1114,"A connector with several kinds of source in one (Lakehouse: Iceberg REST, Unity, Glue or a plain folder, on S3 or\nAzure) has settings that decide what it asks. `tree` is those settings as the connect menu's tree (a catalog,\nand under it the files it can read), each node with the settings its pick gives; give them here\n(`connector_inputs(\"lakehouse\", catalog=\"unity\", files=\"s3\")`) and `inputs` are that combination's.\n`settings` are the ones in force (given, or the kit's default) and `setting_inputs` the setting questions\nthemselves, each with its `choices`, their `choice_labels` and the default in force. Every other connector\nhas an empty `tree` and no `setting_inputs`."],[403,"A CSV, Parquet, JSON or Excel file, a folder of them, or a table already in the database. Files are loaded with the kit's own loader, the one `exakit data-load` runs."],[1022,"A dashboard prepared from an approved dataset and one query."],[1404,"A dashboard prepared from an approved dataset and one query. `preview()` puts it on Dash Server as a preview;\n`confirm(..., figures_checked=True)` publishes it, and only after a person checked the preview's figures."],[364,"A dashboard that goes up as a preview first, and one folder that lets a colleague repeat the work."],[1763,"A dashboard was previewed or published"],[365,"A dashboard, preview first"],[404,"A database or lake elsewhere: PostgreSQL, MySQL, Snowflake and others. The kit connects it as a **virtual schema**: its tables appear in your local Exasol as `VS_<NAME>` and are read from the source when you query them. Nothing is copied."],[1638,"A dataset is one folder in `data/datasets/`. Nothing else names it, so a new folder appears in the menu."],[485,"A dataset that is not loaded yet is loaded first. Nothing else is needed."],[1264,"A dataset the kit offers (`amazon_sales`, `fraud_transactions`): used as it is when it is loaded, else loaded\nfirst with `exakit data-load <id>` (the cell waits for it), then checked against the database. None skips it."],[964,"A dataset the kit offers (`amazon_sales`, `fraud_transactions`): used as it is when it is loaded, else loaded first with `exakit data-load <id>` (the cell waits for it), then checked against the database."],[657,"A dataset the notebooks run on: its descriptor read, validated by the kit's own rules, held against the database, and the roles turned into SQL names, so one notebook runs unchanged on any dataset whose descriptor is valid."],[1612,"A dataset with a column map"],[478,"A dataset with no target skips the model steps and says so. Choose a target in the column map to run them."],[282,"A date or timestamp"],[735,"A descriptor proposed for a table (status draft), or the approved one describe() returned."],[916,"A descriptor proposed for a table (status draft), or the approved one describe() returned."],[286,"A few repeated values"],[1651,"A file already loaded is skipped, not loaded on top of itself."],[1217,"A file loaded as text (every column VARCHAR, as CSVs often are), blank cells, placeholder values and rows copied twice\nall make a result quietly wrong. typed_view() reads the table - not just its names - and proposes one view over it:"],[486,"A file or a folder:"],[1652,"A file that a stopped run left half-written is loaded again from scratch."],[970,"A file that has been loaded but has not yet received an approved descriptor."],[1202,"A file that has been loaded but has not yet received an approved descriptor."],[1765,"A hand-off was written"],[241,"A key is never written into a cell, the code view or the workflow log."],[252,"A kit dataset"],[393,"A kit dataset"],[208,"A kit notebook you did not edit is refreshed when the kit's version changes."],[1732,"A kit notebook you did not edit is refreshed when the kit's version changes."],[1751,"A later notebook continued it"],[1996,"A list of add-on ids, or `\"all\"` or `\"none\"`"],[1992,"A list of dataset ids, or `\"all\"` or `\"none\"`"],[431,"A log that cannot be written warns and the cell goes on. Logging never fails the work it describes."],[1761,"A model call was traced"],[514,"A model is optional. It is used to draft SQL in Ask and to sort texts into themes in Explore. The kit calls an endpoint that speaks the Chat Completions API: an external provider or a model on your own machine."],[38,"A model step is skipped"],[1759,"A model was trained and scored"],[1601,"A new version of the column map, kept under `~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/`, and the roles published on the view `EXAKIT_SEMANTIC.<SCHEMA>__<TABLE>`. The notebooks and AI clients read the approved version from then on."],[159,"A notebook is cells that call the helpers. A card is a form that calls the same helpers. Neither talks to the database on its own."],[1482,"A notebook never needs an id pasted in: the quickstart starts the work and every later notebook continues it with\n`continue_workflow`, which takes this kernel's workflow, else the one inherited through EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID, else the\nlast one started or resumed on this machine ($EXAKIT_HOME/last-workflow), and starts a new one only when there is none."],[1721,"A notebook of your own"],[1743,"A notebook starts a **workflow** and gets an id such as `wf-20261027-3f9a1c`. While it is active, every step the helpers run adds one line to its log. For the idea, see Workflow."],[210,"A notebook you deleted is not copied back."],[1734,"A notebook you deleted is not copied back."],[1733,"A notebook you edited is never overwritten."],[209,"A notebook you edited, or a file of your own, is never overwritten."],[284,"A number to add up or average"],[1950,"A part that fails does not stop the others. The closing line names each part that did not finish and the command that retries it."],[415,"A password inside a connection string is used and never shown."],[413,"A password is asked in a hidden box and handed to `exakit connect` on standard input."],[1447,"A path pasted into a cell, made usable: quotes and spaces around it, a `file://` link, the shell's\nbackslash escapes (`My\\ Data`, from a drag into a terminal) and `~` are undone. Empty stays empty."],[864,"A path pasted into a cell, made usable: quotes and spaces around it, a `file://` link, the shell's backslash escapes (`My\\ Data`, from a drag into a terminal) and `~` are undone."],[1972,"A persona is one file, `personas/<id>.json`, in the kit's repository. No installer code names a persona,