cted, None for a dry run; raises SourceProblem with the kit's reason otherwise."],[1700,"Connect your AI clients to the database, check the connection, and see the skills the kit gives them."],[1815,"Connect your AI clients."],[1446,"connect_source runs `exakit connect <connector> --name <name> ... --password-stdin --yes --json`. The password is\nasked in a hidden box and goes to the command on standard input: never into the cell, the command line or a log."],[585,"Connect, SQL and tracing"],[1564,"Connect, start a workflow and load data: a kit dataset, your own file, or an external source. See Load data."],[1671,"Connection refused"],[1863,"Copy a file into BucketFS and print the path a UDF reads it from."],[1898,"Copy an older kit's container database into this one."],[437,"Correct roles and choose the target"],[299,"Counting rows without repeats"],[1434,"Create and health-check a preview; on Windows use build + healthcheck."],[1239,"Create the view (after the user has read it), describe it, carry the table's roles over and approve them; returns the view's dataset, which the later steps then use."],[1866,"Create, build and deploy a Rust scoring UDF from exported coefficients."],[1484,"Credential-shaped payload keys are checked recursively, including JSON-encoded metadata strings. A secret-named key\nor a DSN containing a password is refused (a\nValueError - the caller's mistake, before anything is written). SQL text is screened rather than refused: a statement\nthat mentions PASSWORD, API_KEY, IDENTIFIED BY and the like - or carries a DSN with a password - is logged with its\ntext replaced by `<redacted: credential-like SQL>` and `redacted: true`, its digest kept, and one warning; the\nlogger never fails the query it records, which has already run. Other SQL text is kept so the user can find the\nquery again."],[1648,"CSV, Parquet and JSON are loaded. JSON is split into tables by an engine the kit installs for you on macOS, Linux and WSL. A `;`-separated CSV is loaded with its delimiter. A tabular `.txt` or `.tsv` file is listed with the rename to `.csv` that the loader needs."],[487,"CSV, Parquet, JSON and Excel work. Leave the schema empty and it is named after the folder: `~/sales-data` becomes `SALES_DATA`."],[614,"Dash Server tools"],[621,"Data checks"],[348,"Data checks, linked tables and the typed, cleaned view - how the data is prepared without ever changing your table."],[362,"Data checks, Schema map and joined view, Typed view."],[1657,"Data in another database is not copied. It is connected with `exakit connect` and read where it lives. See Sources."],[630,"Data map"],[401,"Data reaches the notebooks in three ways. All three end the same way: a table or view the kit can describe, and a column map you approve."],[103,"Data Scientist"],[22,"Data Scientist notebooks"],[1629,"Data Scientist, ML Engineer"],[1632,"Data Scientist, ML Engineer"],[1935,"Data to load"],[243,"Dataset"],[311,"Dataset"],[1616,"Dataset"],[656,"Datasets"],[1609,"Datasets"],[2021,"Datasets"],[80,"Datasets to practise on"],[1966,"Define your own persona"],[928,"Delete what use_model(..., remember=True) saved (the model, Langfuse, or both) and clear it from this kernel."],[1389,"Delete what use_model(..., remember=True) saved (the model, Langfuse, or both) and clear it from this kernel."],[734,"Describe `SCHEMA.TABLE` (or a dataset id's table): the approved descriptor when the table still matches it,\nelse a fresh draft. Uses the connection given, else opens the kit's. Only SELECTs run."],[904,"Describe `SCHEMA.TABLE` (or a dataset id's table): the approved descriptor when the table still matches it, else a fresh draft."],[727,"Describe a table"],[728,"Describe a table from a notebook (DS-2, DS-5): the role-per-column descriptor of setup/lib/descriptor."],[1676,"Describe it first"],[731,"describe() on a table whose approved descriptor still matches it returns that one (force=True profiles again);\notherwise the table is profiled once, in SQL, and e