ap gives every column in a table its role. Its technical name in the code is the descriptor. See Column map and approval."],[711,"The column of a single-column role (entity, category, date, label)."],[1305,"The columns as the pickers show them: low confidence first, then the rest, each in table order."],[1303,"The columns drafted at low confidence, in table order: where the draft guessed, so a person looks first."],[74,"The command that starts, checks, loads and updates everything"],[595,"The connection comes from the kit. Its Jupyter kernel (\"Exasol (Starter Kit)\") carries two paths: the encrypted\nconfiguration store, and the kit's credential file holding the store's master password, readable by the user only.\nThese helpers open the database from there, in JupyterLab, Marimo, VS Code or any front end that runs the\nkit's notebook Python. Nothing here prints or returns a host, a user or a password."],[412,"The connectors, their inputs and the connection-string reader come from the kit's source engine, the one `exakit connect` runs. Nothing about a connector is defined in the notebooks, so a connector added to the kit appears in the form with no notebook change."],[856,"The container behind `alias` runs a smoke UDF, and it has every package training needs."],[578,"The container behind `alias` runs a smoke UDF, and it has every package training needs. The line names the\nalias probed and the fix for that alias (PYTHON3_ML: exakit udf-use default; PYTHON3: exakit udf-setup), so the\nfix installs the container the check looks at. `alias` None is the notebook's default, ml_train.udf_container():\nPYTHON3_ML before PYTHON3 from the kit's manifest, EXAKIT_UDF_CONTAINER first; none installed is a FAIL line."],[1277,"The count column, named after what is counted: ORDER_LINES, STORE_WEEKS; ROW_COUNT when the descriptor does\nnot say (ROWS is an SQL word)."],[884,"The count column, named after what is counted: ORDER_LINES, STORE_WEEKS; ROW_COUNT when the descriptor does not say (ROWS is an SQL word)."],[539,"The dashboard is built from approved roles and a query you can read."],[479,"The data checks, the schema map and the typed view proposal, the group and over-time results with their SQL, a small model with its score, and a note on what the score means."],[340,"The data is checked again, and a column that gives the target away is reported."],[26,"The Data Scientist persona gives you four notebooks that run on the Exasol database on this computer. They are one path with nine steps: get the data in, agree what each column means, prepare, explore, train and check a small model, ask questions in plain language, share a dashboard and hand the work off."],[71,"The database"],[854,"The database answers: its time, this session's id and its version, as one row (and one line)."],[1260,"The database answers: its time, this session's id and its version, as one row (and one line)."],[36,"The database does not answer"],[152,"The database, connections, loading, connectors, add-ons, the describe service"],[724,"The dataset `name`, checked against the database: a kit dataset id, a descriptor file or its folder, or a data\nfile of your own (CSV, Parquet or JSON) with its descriptor beside it, which is loaded first (load_own_file)."],[902,"The dataset `name`, checked against the database: a kit dataset id, a descriptor file or its folder, or a data file of your own (CSV, Parquet or JSON) with its descriptor beside it, which is loaded first (load_own_file)."],[664,"The dataset a notebook works on: `name` when it is set; with None, the one approved last in a quickstart (so\npicking fraud_transactions there carries on here), else amazon_sales. Says which, and why, in one line."],[862,"The dataset a notebook works on: `name` when it is set; with None, the one approved last in a quickstart (so picking fraud_transactions there carries on here), else amazon_sales."],[185,"The dataset approved last, which the notebooks follow"],[59,"The dataset has no text column. `amazon_sales` and `fraud_transactions` have none, so the text model and the themes step skip on them and say so."],[576,"The deployment's bucket directory exists on this machine where the kit says it is, and - given a connection -\na UDF sees it at its /buckets path too (skipped, with a note, when the container check fails)."],[852,"The deployment's bucket directory exists on this machine where the kit says it is, and - given a connection - a UDF sees it at its /buckets path too (skipped, with a note, when the container check fails)."],[761,"The descriptor document (a copy)."],[1200,"The descriptor is that mapping of role to column, a descriptor mapping (`schema_version`, `id`, `fact_table`,\n`roles`), or a descriptor file - YAML or JSON; `data/datasets/<id>/descriptor.yaml` in the kit shows the shape -\nwhose fact_table then names the table (`table` may be None). Given as a mapping of roles, they become a\nschema_version 2 \\*\\*draft\\*\\* (version 1, drafted by the user, owned by EXAKIT_DESCRIPTOR_OWNER or the OS user, its\n`source` the file) and are written beside the file as `<name>.descriptor.yaml` (when no descriptor is there yet),\nso `DATASET = \"<the file>\"` in a notebook opens it again with that one assignment; approving it (the quickstart's\napprove(), or exakit describe \\<id> --approve) is what the training and question steps wait for, exploring does not.\nThe rows travel over pyexasol's import on the open connection: no\nhost, user or password here, as everywhere in exakit.nb. Column types come from the file; the date role's column\nbecomes a DATE and a true/false column 0 or 1; a JSON file is an array of records or one record per line, its nested\nvalues kept as JSON text. The table is marked as loaded from the file (its comment holds the file's SHA-256), so\nrunning the cell again loads nothing when the file is unchanged and reloads it when it changed; a table of the same\nname that this did not create is refused unless `replace=True`."],[687,"The descriptor's `source` as written: a dataset id, `file:<path>`, `vs:<alias>` (or a schema_version 1 file's bare alias), or None."],[1024,"The descriptor's roles, one per line, as the notebook will use them."],[1266,"The descriptor's roles, one per line, as the notebook will use them."],[689,"The descriptor's version: 1 for a first draft or a shipped file; approving writes the next."],[697,"The digest of the table the descriptor was approved on (its `digest` key, design 2.3: sha256 over the table's name, its columns and types, the row count and an order-independent content hash of the role columns), None until approve computes it."],[1504,"The Docs button"],[40,"The documentation does not open"],[789,"The documentation is a site of plain files the kit ships (`notebook/docs/site` in the kit copy): pages, styles and\na search index, built ahead of time. This module serves that folder from this Python on this computer only\n(the loopback address, a free port) and shows it in a frame under the cell, so reading and searching need no internet, no Node\nand no second install. The server starts on the first call and stops with the kernel."],[1722,"The documentation, from a notebook"],[1592,"The draft is deterministic: the same table gives the same draft."],[522,"The endpoint's address"],[1430,"The exact MCP calls an agent makes to create the preview (no credentials)."],[68,"The Exasol Personal Local Starter Kit installs a database on this computer and the tools around it. One command, `exakit`, runs all of it."],[685,"The external source's alias when the table is in a virtual schema (a live source), else None - what confirm_send and the quickstart ask about."],[828,"The feature view is SQL only - category one-hot over the top-20 values plus OTHER, date -> year / month / ISO day of\nweek / days since the first date, text -> LENGTH, entity -> frequency - so a model that is linear over these columns can\nbe scored by Rust on the very same view (ML-5): TF-IDF stays out of it (the client-side model in explore keeps it);\ntop-k token flags computed in SQL are the deferred next step and are recorded as such in the file. The view is not\ncreated here: the ML quickstart and 01_train create it, with the admin profile."],[1980,"The file name without `.json`"],[829,"The file names a table, columns, SQL and digests, never a host, a user or a password; the kit's secret-grep test\ncovers the folder. A workflow that is active gets one `handoff` line in its log (X-1)."],[1116,"The files `exakit data-load` put into the database, as the kit records them (its load receipts): one row per\ntable, the latest load - \\{table, rows, file, loaded_at}. A kit dataset (sample_datasets) is not a file here."],[968,"The files `exakit data-load` put into the database, as the kit records them (its load receipts): one row per table, the latest load - \\{table, rows, file, loaded_at}."],[172,"The files and folders the notebooks read and write on this computer."],[448,"The first argument is the roles you change, the second the slots. With nothing to change, the saved approval stands."],[1520,"The first card of every notebook has a **Docs** button beside the logo. It opens this documentation in a new tab, on the guide for that notebook: loading data from the quickstart, exploring from `01_explore`, asking from `02_ask_your_data`, sharing from `03_share`."],[1527,"The first card of the quickstart is the kit itself. It has two tabs."],[926,"The first dataset that was loaded, in the order given; says which one is used."],[1262,"The first dataset that was loaded, in the order given; says which one is used."],[1974,"The first shows the checks, the question, the answers and the data table. The second then asks the install question live."],[136,"The first writes `notebook/docs/out`; the second copies it to `notebook/docs/site` and stamps it with a digest of the sources."],[745,"The five roles of earlier descriptors, read from the slots: \\{role: column}, \\{text: \\[column]}."],[1677,"The fix is printed first, with the error."],[802,"The folder holds the approved column map (`descriptor.yaml`), the schema map when there is one\n(`schema-map.json`), every query the workflow ran with its digest and row count (`queries.sql`), the workflow log\nas it is (`workflow.jsonl`) and a `README.md` that says what the data is, which column map version the numbers rest\non, which questions were approved, which dashboards were published and how to repeat it. Nothing in it is a password:\nthe log is already written without one, and the connection is the kit's."],[783,"The folder that holds the versions of the descriptor `id` (whether or not it exists yet); an id that is not\na dataset id is refused, so no path is built from it."],[908,"The folder that holds the versions of the descriptor `id` (whether or not it exists yet); an id that is not a dataset id is refused, so no path is built from it."],[1696,"The full reference of an installed add-on is on this computer."],[307,"The groups to compare"],[144,"The guided view"],[156,"The guided view"],[1503,"The guided view"],[366,"The hand-off bundle"],[833,"The handoff as a dict: from a path to the file, from `<id>-v<n>` (that version's file), or from a descriptor\nid (the file with the highest version in the handoffs folder). None there is a FileNotFoundError saying how to\nmake one."],[1008,"The handoff as a dict: from a path to the file, from `<id>-v<n>` (that version's file), or from a descriptor id (the file with the highest version in the handoffs folder)."],[827,"The handoff from the Data Scientist to the ML Engineer (DS-3 -> ML-3, design 4): one JSON file that holds everything\n`01_train` needs to train without opening the descriptor - which descriptor version and digest it came from, a digest\nof the data, the feature view built from the roles (as `CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW` SQL), the label and its positive\nclass, the training SELECT with a reproducible time split, and the input and output schemas. A descriptor without a date\nrole has no time split: the handoff is refused with the fix (`split=\"random\"` for a reproducible hash split, or a\ndate role) - a random split is never silent, and `01_train` refuses one the file does not mark as asked for."],[822,"The handoff from the Data Scientist to the ML Engineer (DS-3 -> ML-3, design 4): one JSON file that holds everything 01_train needs to train without opening the descriptor - which descriptor version and digest it came from, a digest of the data, the feature view built from the roles (as CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW SQL), the label and its positive class, the training SELECT with a reproducible time split, and the input and output schemas."],[830,"The handoff record for `ds` as design 4 shapes it, built now and returned, nothing written: the descriptor's\nid, version, digest (`digest_kind` says whether it is the table digest or the file's) and source; the data\ndigest (`data_digest_kind`); the feature view; the label and its positive class (`label` overrides it);\nthe split (`time` over the date role by default; `split=\"random\"` for a hash split, the only way to get one -\nwithout a date role and without that, a ValueError names the fix; `split.explicit` records the choice) and\n`train_share`; the training SQL; input and output schemas. `workflow_id` defaults to the active workflow's."],[932,"The handoff record for `ds` as design 4 shapes it, built now and returned, nothing written: the descriptor's id, version, digest (`digest_kind` says whether it is the table digest or the file's) and source; the data digest (`data_digest_kind`); the feature view; the label and its positive class (`label` overrides it); the split (`time` over the date role by default; `split=\"random\"` for a hash split, the only way to get one - without a date role and without that, a ValueError names the fix; `split.explicit` records the choice) and `train_share`; the training SQL; input and output schemas."],[1317,"The headless decision for EXAKIT_NB_AUTO_APPROVE=`mode`: `force` approves the proposal; `1` approves only a proposal whose roles equal the current approved version's - then nothing is written (`unchanged`); a proposal that differs stays a `draft` and the reason is printed."],[143,"The helpers"],[153,"The helpers"],[1770,"The helpers refuse a password, a token, a secret or an API key, and a connection string with a password in it. The log never holds a credential."],[141,"The helpers, the guided cards and the kit - which part owns what, and the rules that keep them honest."],[1507,"The Home card"],[1697,"The Home card's **Marketplace** tab does the same with buttons. See Run the kit from a notebook."],[1483,"The id is `wf-YYYYMMDD-<6 hex>`, kept in the session store and in EXAKIT_WORKFLOW_ID so a child process (a CLI call\nfrom a notebook) inherits it. The log is `$EXAKIT_HOME/workflows/<id>.jsonl` (EXAKIT_HOME default\n\\~/.exasol-starter-kit), append-only, one JSON object per line: `{ts, workflow_id, kind, ...payload}`; the folder is\n0700 and the file 0600, each line one O_APPEND write so two kernels on one workflow never interleave. A log that\ncannot be written warns and the cell goes on: logging never fails the work it describes."],[1323,"The ipywidgets picker, or None when this is not a Jupyter kernel with ipywidgets."],[524,"The key"],[1969,"The keys"],[1115,"The kinds of external source `exakit connect` takes, as its own menu lists them (the kit's source engine,\n`catalog`): \\{id, name, summary, aliases, tier, status, version, gate} - `version` the adapter the kit pins,\n`gate` why one is not available yet (empty when it is)."],[880,"The kinds of external source `exakit connect` takes, as its own menu lists them (the kit's source engine, `catalog`): \\{id, name, summary, aliases, tier, status, version, gate} - `version` the adapter the kit pins, `gate` why one is not available yet (empty when it is)."],[150,"The kit"],[62,"The kit and its personas"],[1076,"The kit as it is now, in a few lines: installed or not, the database, each add-on service and its address, the\ndatasets loaded. Never raises: without the command it says where it looked. Returns the status document (\\{} when\nthere is none)."],[940,"The kit as it is now, in a few lines: installed or not, the database, each add-on service and its address, the datasets loaded."],[236,"The kit calls the endpoint you give it: an external provider or a model on your own machine. See Set up a model."],[1615,"The kit carries sample datasets to practise on. `exakit data-load` lists them and loads the ones you pick."],[1706,"The kit connects AI clients to the database through its AI bridge. A client connected this way reads data as the kit's read-only user."],[199,"The kit copy: scripts, datasets, the notebook package and this documentation"],[444,"The kit profiles the table and proposes a role for every column."],[276,"The kit profiles the table in SQL and gives every column one of eight roles, with the evidence that chose it."],[4,"The kit puts an Exasol database on this computer and sets it up for the work you do. What it sets up depends on your **persona**. Pick a section below, or in the list at the top of the sidebar."],[1118,"The kit's notebooks in order (\\{id, persona, step, title, summary, file}), from its notebook catalog; only\n`persona`'s when given. `file` is the path under the notebooks folder (starter-kit-notebooks/...)."],[994,"The kit's notebooks in order (\\{id, persona, step, title, summary, file}), from its notebook catalog; only `persona`'s when given."],[1064,"The kit's own commands, run from a notebook cell with their output shown as it comes - so nobody has to leave the notebook for a terminal to check the kit, update it, install an add-on or load a dataset."],[1111,"The kit's parts as `exakit version --json` reports them: \\{id, installed, available, status, add_on,\nownership, remedy}, with a status of current, ahead, update_available, available (an add-on not installed) or\nmissing; `available` is the version the kit would install or update to."],[868,"The kit's parts as `exakit version --json` reports them: \\{id, installed, available, status, add_on, ownership, remedy}, with a status of current, ahead, update_available, available (an add-on not installed) or missing; `available` is the version the kit would install or update to."],[1000,"The kit's personas (personas/\\*.json): \\{id, title, summary, datasets, addons, visible}."],[1123,"The kit's personas (personas/\\*.json): \\{id, title, summary, datasets, addons, visible}."],[181,"The Marimo versions"],[1107,"The marketplace's add-ons as `exakit marketplace --list --json` reports them: \\{id, name, about, status,\ninstalled, version, url}, and `offered`: False for one the kit's catalog does not offer yet (its\nmarketplace/catalog.json says \"visible\": false, so no marketplace screen lists it)."],[844,"The marketplace's add-ons as `exakit marketplace --list --json` reports them: \\{id, name, about, status, installed, version, url}, and `offered`: False for one the kit's catalog does not offer yet (its marketplace/catalog.json says \"visible\": false, so no marketplace screen lists it)."],[44,"The message is a `DescriptorNotApproved` error. Explore, Ask and Share do not read a draft. Open `00_quickstart` and approve the map. See Review and approve the column map."],[1636,"The ML Engineer persona is not offered in this release, so for now only Data Scientist and General load these datasets."],[389,"The ML Engineer's handoff is a different thing: one JSON file with the feature view, the target and a reproducible split, written by `nb.write_handoff(connection, dataset)` to `~/.exasol-starter-kit/handoffs/`. A stale one is refused, and `nb.handoff_is_stale` names what changed."],[1393,"The MLflow server this kernel records runs to: `tracking_uri` (empty: the kit's own MLflow, or what the shell\nset); `login=True` asks for the server's username and password (hidden). Prints where runs go, never a password."],[1052,"The MLflow server this kernel records runs to: `tracking_uri` (empty: the kit's own MLflow, or what the shell set); `login=True` asks for the server's username and password (hidden)."],[216,"The model is yours"],[1127,"The model lab: nb.model_lab - the Data Scientist chooses the task, the model and the split."],[520,"The model's id"],[529,"The model's id and address can also live in `~/.exasol-starter-kit/exakit.env`. Provider recipes are in `MODEL-PROVIDERS.md`, copied beside the notebooks."],[1690,"The name, the link and the About text of an add-on come from its own repository on GitHub, as last looked up. When a lookup fails, the kit's own copy is shown."],[116,"The new helper now has an entry in its module's reference page and a row in All commands. `nb.docs(nb.your_helper)` opens it once the site is rebuilt."],[341,"The next **version** is written to the kit's store on this computer, under `~/.exasol-starter-kit/descriptors/`."],[1535,"The nine steps"],[1723,"The notebook add-on brings JupyterLab and Marimo, the kit's notebooks and the helpers they use. Install it with a persona that has notebooks, or with `exakit marketplace notebook`."],[475,"The notebook then reads up to 20,000 rows, trains a small baseline model on the category, the entity and the month, scores it on rows it has not seen, and shows what it leans on. `nb.note_model` says in plain words what the score means."],[890,"The notebook's Dash Server tool adapter; each call is an MCP tool call."],[618,"The notebook's Dash Server tool adapter; each call is an MCP tool call. When Dash Server is not installed or\nnot running, it is installed and started first, the way nb.addon_ready(\"dash-server\") does it (`exakit\nmarketplace dash-server`, `exakit start dash-server`), with its progress shown: a cell that previews a dashboard\nworks on its own, and nothing is asked. `ready=False` only reports: it raises when the server is not there."],[1524,"The notebook's own cells sit under **The code behind this page**. In the kit's JupyterLab they are hidden until you choose **Show all the notebook's code cells** at the foot of a card's Code view. In Marimo the cards show stacked, and the cells open with their code visible."],[1531,"The notebooks and the nine steps"],[786,"The notebooks' documentation, opened from a cell: nb.docs()."],[1383,"The optional settings, set from a notebook cell: your model and Langfuse (use_model), the MLflow server (use_mlflow)."],[305,"The outcome to predict"],[494,"The password is asked in a hidden box. It is never part of the code."],[1534,"The path"],[2014,"The personas in this kit"],[1292,"The picker is the descriptor itself: one dropdown per column with the eight roles (key, time, measure, category, flag,\ntext, identifier, other), set to the role the rules drafted and labelled with the evidence that chose it; then one\ndropdown per slot - the columns the notebooks use (key, time, text, target, category, entity) - set to the drafted\ncolumn; then an Approve button. In JupyterLab it is\nipywidgets; in Marimo the review itself is a `mo.ui.dictionary` of `mo.ui.dropdown` with a `mo.ui.run_button`, so\n`ds = review.dataset()` runs again when the button is clicked and stops cleanly (`mo.stop`) until then; in a plain\nPython session `review.approve({\"COLUMN\": \"role\", ...})` is the same path."],[1219,"The proposal for `ds`'s table: its types, its cleaning and the CREATE VIEW, built from the data and the\ndescriptor. Only SELECTs run; nothing is created until `create()`."],[1048,"The proposal for `ds`'s table: its types, its cleaning and the CREATE VIEW, built from the data and the descriptor."],[938,"The proposal for one wide view."],[1335,"The proposal for one wide view. `joins` lists each table it adds and how; `sql` is what create() runs."],[1381,"The proposal: `main` (a dataset, or a table name) with every table its links reach."],[1050,"The proposal."],[1221,"The proposal. `changes` and `cleaning` say what the view does differently from the table, `sql` is the\nCREATE VIEW that `create()` runs - nothing has run before that."],[509,"The quickest way"],[596,"The quickstarts' shared steps (check_connection, list_schemas, load_sample, load_source, ...) are in quickstart.py;\nthe ML Engineer's checks (check_container, check_mlflow, check_bucket) in checks.py."],[733,"The role review (role_picker) speaks the five roles of earlier descriptors - entity, category, date, label, text - so\n`roles`, `evidence`, `missing` and `set(role, column)` read and write the matching slots: date is the time\nslot and label the target."],[758,"The role review's correction: `role` (one of the five) to `column`, or empty with `reason`."],[342,"The roles are published as column comments on a view in the `EXAKIT_SEMANTIC` schema. If publishing fails, the approval still stands and the message says why."],[707,"The roles no column fits, each `{role, reason}`; the notebooks skip what depends on them with the reason."],[749,"The roles no column plays, each with the reason the empty slot gives."],[608,"The rows come over the normal connection rather than pyexasol's HTTP export, which needs the database to connect\nback to this machine - not a given through the local VM or Podman."],[662,"The rules are the kit's descriptor rules (`descriptor_rules`, shipped with this package: the 0.2 kit has no Python\npackage to import them from). It is a copy of tools/descriptor_rules.py, which tools/dataset_check.py uses, and\ntests/test_notebook_contents.py holds the two byte-identical. Nothing is guessed: a descriptor that is invalid, or\nnames a table or column the database lacks, stops the notebook with the reason."],[104,"The same help is built into the kit, so it always matches the version you have."],[1610,"The sample datasets the kit carries, where each comes from, and which persona loads it."],[1018,"The schema as found (a draft) or as approved: `doc` holds its tables and links."],[1360,"The schema as found (a draft) or as approved: `doc` holds its tables and links."],[54,"The schema is not found"],[356,"The schema map shows the tables that link to this one, with the evidence for each link. A link adds the other table's columns without adding rows."],[381,"The schema map, when there is one"],[1333,"The schema of `dataset_or_schema` (a dataset, or a schema name) as found now: its tables, rows and keys, and\nevery many-to-one link between them with its evidence. A live source's schema is not surveyed (its tables are\nqueried in place, every count a round trip)."],[906,"The schema of `dataset_or_schema` (a dataset, or a schema name) as found now: its tables, rows and keys, and every many-to-one link between them with its evidence."],[639,"The semantic map of the database: every table by origin (sample, local, source) with its rows, columns,\ncolumn-map state and roles, then the links between tables - declared, found by an approved schema map, or a\nshared key-like column name across two tables (marked possible). Reads metadata only; returns a DataMap that\nshows itself as a table in a notebook. `include_kit` keeps the kit's own schemas in."],[896,"The semantic map of the database: every table by origin (sample, local, source) with its rows, columns, column-map state and roles, then the links between tables - declared, found by an approved schema map, or a shared key-like column name across two tables (marked possible)."],[512,"The settings behind it"],[28,"The site is a folder of files that ships with the kit. `nb.docs()` serves it from this computer only, so reading and searching work without internet."],[48,"The source refuses the connection or times out"],[1135,"The split is the user's: 50-90% for training, by time (newest held out), random\n(stratified for yes/no) or by group (one group never on both sides), with 3, 5\nor 10 cross-validation folds on the training side. Held-out rows are scored once."],[1258,"The steps both quickstarts share (notebook/notebooks/00_shared): is the database there, what does it hold, and one\nloader per way data comes in - a sample dataset the kit ships, your own file, an external source connected as a\nvirtual schema. Each loader is one cell's call; one that is not set up says so in one line and returns None, so a\nnotebook runs top to bottom whichever ways the user picked."],[1250,"The steps both quickstarts share (notebook/notebooks/00_shared): is the database there, what does it hold, and one loader per way data comes in - a sample dataset the kit ships, your own file, an external source connected as a virtual schema."],[339,"The table has not changed since it was profiled."],[1590,"The table is profiled with SELECTs only. Nothing is written to the database. Every column gets one of eight roles, with its confidence and the evidence that chose it:"],[752,"The table's columns, in table order."],[699,"The table's digest as it is now, computed the way approve computed `table_digest`; a value that differs from `table_digest` means the data changed since the descriptor was approved (a virtual table's digest covers its first sample rows and the row count)."],[207,"The tables of an external source named `<NAME>`"],[713,"The text columns, in the descriptor's order; none when no column plays the text role."],[303,"The text steps"],[1668,"The three faults everyone hits first are turned into what to do:"],[574,"The three things the ML Engineer's notebooks depend on, one check each (ml-engineer/00_quickstart): the database's\nPython container answers a smoke UDF with the packages training needs, the MLflow server is reachable, and the bucket\ndirectory is where the kit expects it. Each prints one line - `ok` with what it found, or `FAIL` with the reason\nand the fix - and returns True or False, so the notebook shows all three before anything stops."],[568,"The three things the ML Engineer's notebooks depend on, one check each (ml-engineer/00_quickstart): the database's Python container answers a smoke UDF